window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2"]={"id":"CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2","title":"CGL 22 OCT 2026 SHIFT 2","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000070881","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Analogy","question":{"en":"If 103 → 1092727, 104 → 1124864, then 105 → ? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि 103 → 1092727, 104 → 1124864 है, तो 105 → ? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1165455"},"2":{"en":"1174100"},"3":{"en":"1165800"},"4":{"en":"1157625"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Each number is replaced by its cube.<br>103<sup>3</sup> = 103 × 103 × 103 = 1092727 ✓<br>104<sup>3</sup> = 104 × 104 × 104 = 1124864 ✓<br>105<sup>3</sup> = 105 × 105 × 105 = 1157625<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 1157625.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक संख्या को उसके घन से बदला गया है।<br>103<sup>3</sup> = 103 × 103 × 103 = 1092727 ✓<br>104<sup>3</sup> = 104 × 104 × 104 = 1124864 ✓<br>105<sup>3</sup> = 105 × 105 × 105 = 1157625<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 1157625 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000070882","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"A shopkeeper marks his goods 20% above the cost price and allows a discount of 10%. Find his gain percent. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक दुकानदार अपने माल पर क्रय मूल्य से 20% अधिक अंकित मूल्य लगाता है और 10% छूट देता है। उसका लाभ प्रतिशत ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15%"},"2":{"en":"12%"},"3":{"en":"10%"},"4":{"en":"8%"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Let the cost price be ₹100.<br>Marked price = 100 + 20% of 100 = ₹120<br>Selling price after 10% discount = 120 × 0.90 = ₹108<br>Gain = 108 − 100 = ₹8 on ₹100, i.e. 8%<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 8%.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए क्रय मूल्य ₹100 है।<br>अंकित मूल्य = 100 + 100 का 20% = ₹120<br>10% छूट के बाद विक्रय मूल्य = 120 × 0.90 = ₹108<br>लाभ = 108 − 100 = ₹100 पर ₹8, अर्थात् 8%<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 8% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000070883","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"Which number should replace the question mark? : <b>1, 2, 6, 24, ?, 720</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न के स्थान पर कौन-सी संख्या आनी चाहिए? : <b>1, 2, 6, 24, ?, 720</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"100"},"2":{"en":"150"},"3":{"en":"120"},"4":{"en":"144"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The terms are factorials:<br>1 = 1!<br>2 = 2!<br>6 = 3!<br>24 = 4!<br>? = 5! = 5 × 4 × 3 × 2 × 1 = 120<br>720 = 6!<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 120.</b>","hi":"पद क्रमगुणित (factorial) हैं:<br>1 = 1!<br>2 = 2!<br>6 = 3!<br>24 = 4!<br>? = 5! = 5 × 4 × 3 × 2 × 1 = 120<br>720 = 6!<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 120 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000070884","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"In a group of 40 children, 28 like Ice Cream, 18 like Cake, and 10 like both. How many children like only Cake? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"40 बच्चों के एक समूह में 28 को आइसक्रीम पसंद है, 18 को केक पसंद है और 10 को दोनों पसंद हैं। कितने बच्चों को केवल केक पसंद है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"10"},"2":{"en":"8"},"3":{"en":"18"},"4":{"en":"28"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Children who like both = 10<br>Children who like cake = 18<br>Only cake = 18 − 10 = 8<br>(Check: only ice cream = 28 − 10 = 18, and 18 + 10 + 8 = 36, so 4 children like neither, which is within the total of 40.)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 8.</b>","hi":"दोनों पसंद करने वाले बच्चे = 10<br>केक पसंद करने वाले बच्चे = 18<br>केवल केक = 18 − 10 = 8<br>(जाँच: केवल आइसक्रीम = 28 − 10 = 18, तथा 18 + 10 + 8 = 36, अतः 4 बच्चों को कुछ भी पसंद नहीं, जो कुल 40 के भीतर है।)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 8 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000070885","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code if CLEAR is coded as DMFBS, how is DMFBS coded? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"किसी कूट भाषा में यदि CLEAR को DMFBS लिखा जाता है, तो DMFBS को कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"ENGCT"},"2":{"en":"DMFCT"},"3":{"en":"ENFCS"},"4":{"en":"CLEAR"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Each letter is replaced by the next letter of the alphabet:<br>C → D, L → M, E → F, A → B, R → S<br>Applying the same rule to DMFBS:<br>D → E, M → N, F → G, B → C, S → T<br>So the code is ENGCT.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): ENGCT.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक अक्षर को वर्णमाला के अगले अक्षर से बदला गया है:<br>C → D, L → M, E → F, A → B, R → S<br>यही नियम DMFBS पर लगाने पर:<br>D → E, M → N, F → G, B → C, S → T<br>अतः कूट ENGCT है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): ENGCT है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000070886","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"In the sequence, what follows next: <b>2P, 5M, 10J, 17G, ?</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"इस श्रृंखला में अगला पद क्या है: <b>2P, 5M, 10J, 17G, ?</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"22 O"},"2":{"en":"24 P"},"3":{"en":"26 D"},"4":{"en":"11 M"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Numbers: 2, 5, 10, 17 → the differences are 3, 5, 7; the next difference is 9, so 17 + 9 = 26.<br>Letters: P(16), M(13), J(10), G(7) → each letter is 3 places before the previous one; next = G − 3 = D(4).<br>So the next term is 26 D.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 26 D.</b>","hi":"संख्याएँ: 2, 5, 10, 17 → अंतर 3, 5, 7 है; अगला अंतर 9 होगा, अतः 17 + 9 = 26।<br>अक्षर: P(16), M(13), J(10), G(7) → प्रत्येक अक्षर पिछले से 3 स्थान पीछे है; अगला = G − 3 = D(4)।<br>अतः अगला पद 26 D है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 26 D है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000070887","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, “PLANNER” is written as “SFOOBMQ.” How will “DRAWING” be written? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"किसी कूट भाषा में “PLANNER” को “SFOOBMQ” लिखा जाता है। “DRAWING” को कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"HOIXBSE"},"2":{"en":"HOXIBSF"},"3":{"en":"HOXJBSF"},"4":{"en":"HOJXBSE"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"First write the word in reverse order and then move every letter one step forward in the alphabet.<br>PLANNER → reversed = RENNALP<br>R → S, E → F, N → O, N → O, A → B, L → M, P → Q → SFOOBMQ ✓<br>DRAWING → reversed = GNIWARD<br>G → H, N → O, I → J, W → X, A → B, R → S, D → E → HOJXBSE<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): HOJXBSE.</b>","hi":"पहले शब्द को उल्टे क्रम में लिखिए और फिर प्रत्येक अक्षर को वर्णमाला में एक स्थान आगे बढ़ाइए।<br>PLANNER → उल्टा = RENNALP<br>R → S, E → F, N → O, N → O, A → B, L → M, P → Q → SFOOBMQ ✓<br>DRAWING → उल्टा = GNIWARD<br>G → H, N → O, I → J, W → X, A → B, R → S, D → E → HOJXBSE<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): HOJXBSE है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000070888","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Four options are given below, out of which three are similar in a certain way while one is different. Identify the option that is different from the others. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"नीचे चार विकल्प दिए गए हैं, जिनमें से तीन किसी प्रकार समान हैं जबकि एक भिन्न है। वह विकल्प पहचानिए जो अन्य से भिन्न है। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Fleet"},"2":{"en":"Convoy"},"3":{"en":"Armada"},"4":{"en":"Caravan"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"A fleet, a convoy and an armada are all groups of ships (naval/sea-going vessels).<br>A caravan is a group of travellers, camels or vehicles moving together on land, not on water.<br>So ‘Caravan’ is different from the other three.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Caravan.</b>","hi":"फ्लीट (fleet), कॉनवॉय (convoy) और आर्माडा (armada) — ये सभी जलयानों (जहाज़ों) के समूह हैं।<br>कैरवान (caravan) स्थल पर एक साथ चलने वाले यात्रियों, ऊँटों या वाहनों का समूह है, जल पर नहीं।<br>अतः ‘Caravan’ शेष तीन से भिन्न है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): Caravan है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000070889","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"A + B means A is the father of B. A = B means A is the wife of B. A × B means A is the brother of B. A ÷ B means A is the daughter of B.<br>If <b>P ÷ R + S + Q</b>, which of the following is true? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"A + B का अर्थ है A, B का पिता है। A = B का अर्थ है A, B की पत्नी है। A × B का अर्थ है A, B का भाई है। A ÷ B का अर्थ है A, B की पुत्री है।<br>यदि <b>P ÷ R + S + Q</b> है, तो निम्नलिखित में से क्या सत्य है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"P is the daughter of Q.","hi":"P, Q की पुत्री है।"},"2":{"en":"Q is the aunt of P.","hi":"Q, P की आंटी है।"},"3":{"en":"P is the aunt of Q.","hi":"P, Q की आंटी है।"},"4":{"en":"P is the mother of Q.","hi":"P, Q की माता है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"162\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 162\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"109\" y=\"62\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"161\" y=\"116\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M146 28V50M122 50H171M122 50V62M171 50V62M171 82V104M171 104V116\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"146\" y=\"22\">R+</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"76\">P−</text><text x=\"171\" y=\"76\">S+</text><text x=\"171\" y=\"130\">Q</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"157\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></svg><br>P is the sister of Q's father S, so P is Q's aunt.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): P is the aunt of Q..</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"162\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 162\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"109\" y=\"62\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"161\" y=\"116\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M146 28V50M122 50H171M122 50V62M171 50V62M171 82V104M171 104V116\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"146\" y=\"22\">R+</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"76\">P−</text><text x=\"171\" y=\"76\">S+</text><text x=\"171\" y=\"130\">Q</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"157\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ पुरुष  − स्त्री  — भाई-बहन  = पति-पत्नी  | पीढ़ी</text></svg><br>P, Q के पिता S की बहन है, अतः P, Q की बुआ है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): P, Q की आंटी है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000070890","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Study the pattern in the given series and find the next set of letters in the series.<br><b>FIE, IHH, LGK, OFN, ?</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दी गई श्रृंखला में पैटर्न का अध्ययन कीजिए और श्रृंखला में अक्षरों का अगला समूह ज्ञात कीजिए।<br><b>FIE, IHH, LGK, OFN, ?</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"REQ"},"2":{"en":"RDF"},"3":{"en":"REG"},"4":{"en":"PEG"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"First letters: F(6), I(9), L(12), O(15) → +3 each time; next = O + 3 = R(18).<br>Second letters: I(9), H(8), G(7), F(6) → −1 each time; next = F − 1 = E(5).<br>Third letters: E(5), H(8), K(11), N(14) → +3 each time; next = N + 3 = Q(17).<br>So the next set is REQ.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): REQ.</b>","hi":"पहले अक्षर: F(6), I(9), L(12), O(15) → हर बार +3; अगला = O + 3 = R(18)।<br>दूसरे अक्षर: I(9), H(8), G(7), F(6) → हर बार −1; अगला = F − 1 = E(5)।<br>तीसरे अक्षर: E(5), H(8), K(11), N(14) → हर बार +3; अगला = N + 3 = Q(17)।<br>अतः अगला समूह REQ है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): REQ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000070891","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Completing","question":{"en":"Complete the pattern in fig. (X) by selecting one of the figures from the four alternatives :<br>Figure(X):<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q11.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"चार विकल्पों में से एक आकृति चुनकर आकृति (X) में पैटर्न पूरा करें :<br>आकृति (X):<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q11.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In fig. (X) the four cells contain a triangle, a square and a hexagon, each with a dot inside, and the question mark stands for the fourth figure of the same family.<br>The number of sides increases in the order triangle (3) → square (4) → pentagon (5) → hexagon (6), and in every figure a dot is placed inside the shape.<br>The missing figure must therefore be a pentagon with a dot inside it, which is alternative (A).<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1).</b>","hi":"आकृति (X) के चारों खानों में एक त्रिभुज, एक वर्ग तथा एक षट्भुज है, जिनमें से प्रत्येक के भीतर एक बिंदु है, और प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न उसी श्रेणी की चौथी आकृति को दर्शाता है।<br>भुजाओं की संख्या इस क्रम में बढ़ती है — त्रिभुज (3) → वर्ग (4) → पंचभुज (5) → षट्भुज (6), और प्रत्येक आकृति के भीतर एक बिंदु है।<br>अतः लुप्त आकृति में एक बिंदु के साथ पंचभुज होना चाहिए, जो विकल्प (A) है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q11.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q11_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q11_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q11_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q11_opt4.jpg"]}}},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000070892","section":"REASONING","topic":"Order & Ranking","question":{"en":"Arrange the following according to the stages of construction.<br>1. Painting<br>2. Designing<br>3. Foundation<br>4. Roofing [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित को निर्माण के चरणों के अनुसार व्यवस्थित कीजिए।<br>1. पुताई (पेंटिंग)<br>2. डिज़ाइनिंग<br>3. नींव (फाउंडेशन)<br>4. छत (रूफिंग) [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2, 3, 4, 1"},"2":{"en":"3, 2, 4, 1"},"3":{"en":"2, 4, 3, 1"},"4":{"en":"3, 4, 2, 1"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"A building is first designed and then constructed:<br>First — Designing (2)<br>Next — Foundation (3)<br>Then — Roofing (4)<br>Finally — Painting (1)<br>So the correct order is 2, 3, 4, 1.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 2, 3, 4, 1.</b>","hi":"भवन का निर्माण पहले डिज़ाइन करके फिर किया जाता है:<br>पहले — डिज़ाइनिंग (2)<br>फिर — नींव (3)<br>उसके बाद — छत (4)<br>अंत में — पुताई (1)<br>अतः सही क्रम 2, 3, 4, 1 है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 2, 3, 4, 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000070893","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which of the following centre code does not maintain the pattern of “one letter followed by three digits”? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा सेंटर कोड “एक अक्षर के बाद तीन अंक” के पैटर्न का पालन नहीं करता? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A123"},"2":{"en":"B456"},"3":{"en":"789C"},"4":{"en":"D012"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The required pattern is: a letter first and then three digits.<br>A123 → letter A + 123 digits ✓<br>B456 → letter B + 456 digits ✓<br>D012 → letter D + 012 digits ✓<br>789C → three digits 789 followed by the letter C — the order is reversed, so this code does not follow the pattern.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 789C.</b>","hi":"अभीष्ट पैटर्न है: पहले एक अक्षर और फिर तीन अंक।<br>A123 → अक्षर A + 123 अंक ✓<br>B456 → अक्षर B + 456 अंक ✓<br>D012 → अक्षर D + 012 अंक ✓<br>789C → पहले तीन अंक 789 और फिर अक्षर C — क्रम उल्टा है, इसलिए यह कोड पैटर्न का पालन नहीं करता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 789C है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000070894","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">21</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">27</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">36</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">18</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">54</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार किसी निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। इस पैटर्न को पहचानिए और तदनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">21</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">27</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">36</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">18</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">54</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"18"},"2":{"en":"24"},"3":{"en":"36"},"4":{"en":"48"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In every row the third and the fourth numbers are obtained by multiplying the first and the second numbers by the same number.<br>Row 1: 7 × 3 = 21 and 9 × 3 = 27 (multiplier 3)<br>Row 2: 4 × 9 = 36 and 2 × 9 = 18 (multiplier 9)<br>Row 3: 9 × 6 = 54, so the missing number = 4 × 6 = 24<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 24.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पंक्ति में तीसरी और चौथी संख्या पहली और दूसरी संख्या को एक ही संख्या से गुणा करके प्राप्त होती है।<br>पंक्ति 1: 7 × 3 = 21 तथा 9 × 3 = 27 (गुणक 3)<br>पंक्ति 2: 4 × 9 = 36 तथा 2 × 9 = 18 (गुणक 9)<br>पंक्ति 3: 9 × 6 = 54, अतः लुप्त संख्या = 4 × 6 = 24<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 24 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000070895","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If 9 @ 3 = 54 and 7 @ 2 = 35, what is the value of 11 @ 4? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि 9 @ 3 = 54 तथा 7 @ 2 = 35 है, तो 11 @ 4 का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"64"},"2":{"en":"72"},"3":{"en":"77"},"4":{"en":"88"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The rule is: A @ B = A × (A − B)<br>9 @ 3 = 9 × (9 − 3) = 9 × 6 = 54 ✓<br>7 @ 2 = 7 × (7 − 2) = 7 × 5 = 35 ✓<br>11 @ 4 = 11 × (11 − 4) = 11 × 7 = 77<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 77.</b>","hi":"नियम है: A @ B = A × (A − B)<br>9 @ 3 = 9 × (9 − 3) = 9 × 6 = 54 ✓<br>7 @ 2 = 7 × (7 − 2) = 7 × 5 = 35 ✓<br>11 @ 4 = 11 × (11 − 4) = 11 × 7 = 77<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 77 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000070896","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>A public library has introduced a new service that allows members to check out tablets and e-readers in addition to traditional books.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. The library considers digital learning resources to be useful for its members.<br>II. The library has decided to discontinue lending printed books. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए गए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच कीजिए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष, यदि कोई हो, कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता/निकलते है/हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>एक सार्वजनिक पुस्तकालय ने एक नई सेवा शुरू की है जिससे सदस्य पारंपरिक पुस्तकों के अतिरिक्त टैबलेट और ई-रीडर भी ले जा सकते हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. पुस्तकालय डिजिटल शिक्षण संसाधनों को अपने सदस्यों के लिए उपयोगी मानता है।<br>II. पुस्तकालय ने मुद्रित पुस्तकों का वितरण बंद करने का निर्णय लिया है। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Either conclusion I or II follows","hi":"या तो निष्कर्ष I या II निकलता है"},"4":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II निकलता है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The library is adding tablets and e-readers to its collection, which shows that it regards digital learning resources as useful for its members — conclusion I follows.<br>The statement says the new service is ‘in addition to traditional books’, so lending of printed books continues — conclusion II does not follow.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only conclusion I follows.</b>","hi":"पुस्तकालय अपने संग्रह में टैबलेट और ई-रीडर जोड़ रहा है, जिससे स्पष्ट है कि वह डिजिटल शिक्षण संसाधनों को सदस्यों के लिए उपयोगी मानता है — निष्कर्ष I निकलता है।<br>कथन कहता है कि नई सेवा ‘पारंपरिक पुस्तकों के अतिरिक्त’ है, अतः मुद्रित पुस्तकों का वितरण जारी रहता है — निष्कर्ष II नहीं निकलता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000070897","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>England have received a boost with Jofra Archer back in the squad after serving his suspension for the final Test. He was unavailable for the second Test due to a breach of COVID-19 protocols, but his absence did not harm England’s performance as much as had been anticipated.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Archer was suspended for applying saliva to the ball in violation of new playing rules introduced by the COVID-19 pandemic.<br>II. England was able to secure a favourable result in the second test match. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए गए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच कीजिए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष, यदि कोई हो, कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता/निकलते है/हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>अंतिम टेस्ट के लिए अपना निलंबन पूरा करने के बाद जोफ्रा आर्चर के टीम में लौटने से इंग्लैंड को बल मिला है। COVID-19 प्रोटोकॉल के उल्लंघन के कारण वे दूसरे टेस्ट के लिए उपलब्ध नहीं थे, परंतु उनकी अनुपस्थिति ने इंग्लैंड के प्रदर्शन को उतनी हानि नहीं पहुँचाई जितनी आशंका थी।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. आर्चर को COVID-19 महामारी के कारण लागू नए खेल नियमों के उल्लंघन में गेंद पर थूक लगाने के लिए निलंबित किया गया था।<br>II. इंग्लैंड दूसरे टेस्ट मैच में अनुकूल परिणाम प्राप्त करने में सफल रहा। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II निकलता है"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The statement says only that Archer’s absence ‘did not harm England’s performance as much as had been anticipated’, which means England performed well in that Test and came out with a favourable result — conclusion II follows.<br>The reason for the suspension is not given in the statement, so the specific claim about saliva cannot be drawn from it — conclusion I does not follow.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Only conclusion II follows.</b>","hi":"कथन केवल इतना कहता है कि आर्चर की अनुपस्थिति ने इंग्लैंड के प्रदर्शन को ‘उतनी हानि नहीं पहुँचाई जितनी आशंका थी’, अर्थात् उस टेस्ट में इंग्लैंड ने अच्छा प्रदर्शन किया और अनुकूल परिणाम प्राप्त किया — निष्कर्ष II निकलता है।<br>निलंबन का कारण कथन में नहीं दिया गया, इसलिए गेंद पर थूक लगाने का विशिष्ट दावा कथन से नहीं निकाला जा सकता — निष्कर्ष I नहीं निकलता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000070898","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"In the following question, one statement is given, followed by certain inferences. Consider the statement to be true even if it seems to contradict commonly known facts. Read the inferences carefully and decide which of them logically follow from the given statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>The municipal corporation has warned that citizens caught wasting water by washing cars or driveways with hosepipes during the peak summer months will face a heavy penalty of ₹5,000.<br><b>Inferences:</b><br>I. The city is likely facing a water scarcity or supply crunch during the summer.<br>II. Imposing a fine of ₹5,000 will completely stop the wastage of water in the city. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन दिया गया है, जिसके बाद कुछ अनुमान हैं। कथन को सत्य मानिए, चाहे वह सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों के विपरीत प्रतीत हो। अनुमानों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि उनमें से कौन-से कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>नगर निगम ने चेतावनी दी है कि गर्मियों के चरम महीनों में नली से कार या ड्राइववे धोकर पानी बर्बाद करते पकड़े गए नागरिकों पर ₹5,000 का भारी जुर्माना लगाया जाएगा।<br><b>अनुमान:</b><br>I. शहर में गर्मियों के दौरान जल की कमी या आपूर्ति संकट होने की संभावना है।<br>II. ₹5,000 का जुर्माना लगाने से शहर में पानी की बर्बादी पूरी तरह रुक जाएगी। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Neither Inference I nor Inference II follows.","hi":"न तो अनुमान I और न ही अनुमान II निकलता है।"},"2":{"en":"Only Inference II follows.","hi":"केवल अनुमान II निकलता है।"},"3":{"en":"Both Inferences I and II follow.","hi":"अनुमान I और II दोनों निकलते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Only Inference I follows.","hi":"केवल अनुमान I निकलता है।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Such a heavy penalty is imposed only when water is scarce, so the city is very likely facing a water scarcity or supply crunch in summer — inference I follows.<br>A fine may reduce wastage, but it cannot be said that it will ‘completely stop’ the wastage of water — inference II is too absolute and does not follow.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Only Inference I follows.</b>","hi":"इतना भारी जुर्माना तभी लगाया जाता है जब पानी की कमी हो, अतः शहर में गर्मियों में जल की कमी या आपूर्ति संकट होने की पूरी संभावना है — अनुमान I निकलता है।<br>जुर्माना बर्बादी घटा सकता है, परंतु यह नहीं कहा जा सकता कि पानी की बर्बादी ‘पूरी तरह’ रुक जाएगी — अनुमान II अत्यधिक है और नहीं निकलता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): केवल अनुमान I निकलता है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000070899","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"A multinational corporation has identified excessive paper usage as a significant contributor to operational cost and environmental waste. The management has decided to implement a long-term sustainability strategy aimed at minimizing dependence on physical documents while maintaining efficiency and accessibility of records.<br>Which of the following policies would most effectively help the organization achieve this objective? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक बहुराष्ट्रीय कंपनी ने अत्यधिक कागज़ के उपयोग को परिचालन लागत तथा पर्यावरणीय अपव्यय का महत्वपूर्ण कारण पहचाना है। प्रबंधन ने दीर्घकालिक स्थिरता रणनीति लागू करने का निर्णय लिया है, जिसका उद्देश्य अभिलेखों की दक्षता और उपलब्धता बनाए रखते हुए भौतिक दस्तावेज़ों पर निर्भरता कम करना है।<br>निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी नीति संगठन को यह उद्देश्य सबसे प्रभावी रूप से प्राप्त करने में सहायता करेगी? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Require employees to print all electronic communications and correspondence for record-keeping purposes.","hi":"अभिलेख रखने के उद्देश्य से सभी इलेक्ट्रॉनिक संचार और पत्राचार को प्रिंट करने का निर्देश दें।"},"2":{"en":"Increase the procurement of paper supplies to ensure uninterrupted availability across departments.","hi":"सभी विभागों में निर्बाध उपलब्धता सुनिश्चित करने के लिए कागज़ की खरीद बढ़ाएँ।"},"3":{"en":"Transition to a comprehensive digital documentation system for storing, sharing, and managing organizational records.","hi":"संगठनात्मक अभिलेखों के भंडारण, साझाकरण तथा प्रबंधन के लिए एक व्यापक डिजिटल दस्तावेज़ प्रणाली अपनाएँ।"},"4":{"en":"Mandate the creation of multiple hard-copy duplicates of every official document.","hi":"प्रत्येक आधिकारिक दस्तावेज़ की कई हार्ड कॉपी बनाना अनिवार्य कर दें।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The objective is to reduce dependence on physical paper while keeping records efficient and accessible.<br>Moving to a comprehensive digital documentation system directly reduces paper use and, at the same time, keeps records easy to store, search and share.<br>Printing more, buying more paper or making multiple hard copies will only increase paper usage, which is the very problem to be solved.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Transition to a comprehensive digital documentation system for storing, sharing, and managing organizational records.</b>","hi":"उद्देश्य यह है कि अभिलेखों को दक्ष और सुलभ रखते हुए कागज़ पर निर्भरता कम की जाए।<br>व्यापक डिजिटल दस्तावेज़ प्रणाली अपनाने से कागज़ का उपयोग सीधे कम होता है और साथ ही अभिलेखों को संग्रहित, खोजने और साझा करने में सुविधा बनी रहती है।<br>अधिक प्रिंट करना, अधिक कागज़ खरीदना या कई हार्ड कॉपी बनाना कागज़ के उपयोग को और बढ़ाएगा, जो स्वयं समस्या है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): संगठनात्मक अभिलेखों के भंडारण, साझाकरण तथा प्रबंधन के लिए एक व्यापक डिजिटल दस्तावेज़ प्रणाली अपनाएँ।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000070900","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the following question, three statements are given, followed by two conclusions. Consider the statements to be true even if they differ from commonly known facts. Read the conclusions carefully and decide which of the conclusions logically follow from the given statements.<br><b>Statements:</b><br>Only a few files are folders.<br>Some folders are documents.<br>No document is a book.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. All files can be folders is a possibility.<br>II. All folders can be files is a possibility. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में तीन कथन दिए गए हैं, जिनके बाद दो निष्कर्ष हैं। कथनों को सत्य मानिए, चाहे वे सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों से भिन्न हों। निष्कर्षों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-से निष्कर्ष दिए गए कथनों से तार्किक रूप से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>केवल कुछ फाइलें, फोल्डर हैं।<br>कुछ फोल्डर, दस्तावेज़ हैं।<br>कोई भी दस्तावेज़, पुस्तक नहीं है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. सभी फाइलें, फोल्डर हो सकती हैं, यह संभावना है।<br>II. सभी फोल्डर, फाइलें हो सकते हैं, यह संभावना है। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Either conclusion I or conclusion II follows","hi":"या तो निष्कर्ष I या निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"‘Only a few files are folders’ means some files are folders and the remaining files are definitely not folders.<br>So the possibility ‘all files are folders’ is ruled out — conclusion I does not follow.<br>There is no such restriction on folders, so the possibility ‘all folders are files’ remains open — conclusion II follows.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Only conclusion II follows.</b>","hi":"‘केवल कुछ फाइलें, फोल्डर हैं’ का अर्थ है कि कुछ फाइलें फोल्डर हैं और शेष फाइलें निश्चित रूप से फोल्डर नहीं हैं।<br>इसलिए ‘सभी फाइलें, फोल्डर हैं’ की संभावना समाप्त हो जाती है — निष्कर्ष I नहीं निकलता।<br>फोल्डर पर ऐसा कोई प्रतिबंध नहीं है, अतः ‘सभी फोल्डर, फाइलें हो सकते हैं’ की संभावना बनी रहती है — निष्कर्ष II निकलता है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000070901","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"Identify the Venn diagram that accurately depicts the logical relationships between the given categories.<br><b>Table, Transistor, Furniture</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"वह वेन आरेख पहचानिए जो दिए गए वर्गों के बीच तार्किक संबंधों को सही रूप से दर्शाता है।<br><b>मेज़ (Table), ट्रांजिस्टर, फर्नीचर</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"A table is a kind of furniture, so the circle of ‘table’ must lie completely inside the circle of ‘furniture’.<br>A transistor is an electronic component and has nothing to do with furniture, so its circle must be completely separate.<br>Only the diagram of option (2) shows one ellipse (table) inside another ellipse (furniture) while the third ellipse (transistor) is kept apart.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2).</b>","hi":"मेज़, फर्नीचर का ही एक प्रकार है, इसलिए ‘मेज़’ का वृत्त ‘फर्नीचर’ के वृत्त के पूर्णतः भीतर होना चाहिए।<br>ट्रांजिस्टर एक इलेक्ट्रॉनिक घटक है और फर्नीचर से इसका कोई संबंध नहीं, इसलिए उसका वृत्त पूर्णतः अलग होना चाहिए।<br>केवल विकल्प (2) के आरेख में एक दीर्घवृत्त (मेज़) दूसरे दीर्घवृत्त (फर्नीचर) के भीतर है तथा तीसरा दीर्घवृत्त (ट्रांजिस्टर) अलग है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q21_opt4.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q21_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q21_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q21_opt1.jpg"]}}},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000070902","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"To address the significant decline in foot traffic at the downtown shopping district, the local chamber of commerce has proposed pedestrianizing the area to encourage leisure walking. Which assumption underlies this proposal? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"डाउनटाउन शॉपिंग जिले में पैदल आने-जाने वालों की संख्या में महत्वपूर्ण गिरावट को दूर करने के लिए स्थानीय चैंबर ऑफ कॉमर्स ने आराम से टहलने को प्रोत्साहित करने हेतु क्षेत्र को पैदल-मात्र क्षेत्र बनाने का प्रस्ताव रखा है। इस प्रस्ताव के पीछे कौन-सी पूर्वधारणा है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Pedestrian-only zones significantly increase the likelihood of spontaneous spending by casual visitors.","hi":"पैदल-मात्र क्षेत्र आकस्मिक आगंतुकों द्वारा स्वतः खर्च करने की संभावना को महत्वपूर्ण रूप से बढ़ाते हैं।"},"2":{"en":"The lack of pedestrian access is the single most important factor deterring shoppers from the area.","hi":"पैदल पहुँच की कमी ही खरीदारों को इस क्षेत्र से दूर रखने वाला सबसे महत्वपूर्ण कारक है।"},"3":{"en":"Every business located in the downtown district is capable of adapting their storefront for pedestrians.","hi":"डाउनटाउन जिले में स्थित प्रत्येक व्यवसाय अपने स्टोरफ्रंट को पैदल चलने वालों के अनुकूल बनाने में सक्षम है।"},"4":{"en":"Implementing this change will immediately restore the district to its peak historical sales levels.","hi":"इस परिवर्तन को लागू करने से जिला तुरंत अपने ऐतिहासिक बिक्री स्तर तक पहुँच जाएगा।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The proposal is meant to raise foot traffic, which in turn is expected to bring more business — so the proposal assumes that more pedestrians will mean more spontaneous spending by casual visitors.<br>Option (2) is too strong (‘single most important factor’), option (3) talks about storefronts and option (4) promises immediate restoration of peak sales, which nobody can assume.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Pedestrian-only zones significantly increase the likelihood of spontaneous spending by casual visitors.</b>","hi":"प्रस्ताव का उद्देश्य पैदल आने-जाने वालों की संख्या बढ़ाना है, जिससे अधिक व्यवसाय की अपेक्षा है — अतः प्रस्ताव यह मानता है कि अधिक पैदल आगंतुकों का अर्थ है आकस्मिक आगंतुकों द्वारा अधिक स्वतः खर्च।<br>विकल्प (2) अत्यधिक है (‘सबसे महत्वपूर्ण कारक’), विकल्प (3) स्टोरफ्रंट की बात करता है और विकल्प (4) तुरंत चरम बिक्री स्तर की बात करता है, जिसकी पूर्वधारणा कोई नहीं कर सकता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): पैदल-मात्र क्षेत्र आकस्मिक आगंतुकों द्वारा स्वतः खर्च करने की संभावना को महत्वपूर्ण रूप से बढ़ाते हैं।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000070903","section":"REASONING","topic":"Paper Folding, Cutting & Mirror/Water Images","question":{"en":"Choose the alternative which most closely resembles the mirror image of the given combination when mirror is placed at the right side of the image.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q23.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"वह विकल्प चुनिए जो दी गई आकृति का दर्पण प्रतिबिंब सबसे अधिक मिलता-जुलता हो, जब दर्पण को आकृति के दाईं ओर रखा जाए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q23.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"When the mirror is on the right side, the left and the right of the figure get interchanged while the top and the bottom remain unchanged.<br>So the solid black block that is at the top-left of the question figure must appear at the top-right, the arrow pointing upwards remains pointing upwards while the small arrow beside it turns to point towards the left, and the ellipse inside the lower box must shift to the opposite side.<br>Only alternative (B) shows all these changes correctly.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2).</b>","hi":"जब दर्पण दाईं ओर हो, तो आकृति का बायाँ और दायाँ भाग परस्पर बदल जाता है तथा ऊपर-नीचे जैसा है वैसा रहता है।<br>अतः प्रश्न आकृति के ऊपर-बाएँ स्थित ठोस काला खंड ऊपर-दाएँ आ जाएगा, ऊपर की ओर इंगित तीर ऊपर ही रहेगा जबकि उसके पास वाला छोटा तीर बाईं ओर इंगित करेगा, और नीचे के बक्से के भीतर का दीर्घवृत्त विपरीत दिशा में आ जाएगा।<br>केवल विकल्प (B) में ये सभी परिवर्तन सही ढंग से दिखाए गए हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q23.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q23_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q23_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q23_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q23_opt4.jpg"]}}},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000070904","section":"REASONING","topic":"Paper Folding, Cutting & Mirror/Water Images","question":{"en":"Choose the alternative which most closely resembles the mirror image of the given combination when mirror PQ is placed at the right side of the image.<br>3 4 6 5 1 2<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q24.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"वह विकल्प चुनिए जो दी गई संख्या-श्रृंखला का दर्पण प्रतिबिंब सबसे अधिक मिलता-जुलता हो, जब दर्पण PQ को आकृति के दाईं ओर रखा जाए।<br>3 4 6 5 1 2<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q24.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"With the mirror on the right, the order of the digits is reversed and every digit is laterally inverted: 3 4 6 5 1 2 → 2 1 5 6 4 3 with each digit turned left-to-right.<br>Option (1) has the digits in the wrong order, option (3) contains a wrongly drawn digit and option (4) is not laterally inverted but simply shifted.<br>Only alternative (B) shows the reversed order with each digit correctly laterally inverted.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2).</b>","hi":"दर्पण दाईं ओर होने पर अंकों का क्रम उलट जाता है और प्रत्येक अंक पार्श्व-विपरीत हो जाता है: 3 4 6 5 1 2 → 2 1 5 6 4 3, प्रत्येक अंक बाएँ-दाएँ पलटा हुआ।<br>विकल्प (1) में अंकों का क्रम गलत है, विकल्प (3) में एक अंक गलत बना है और विकल्प (4) पार्श्व-विपरीत नहीं बल्कि केवल खिसका हुआ है।<br>केवल विकल्प (B) में उल्टा क्रम तथा प्रत्येक अंक सही रूप से पार्श्व-विपरीत दिखाया गया है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q24.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q24_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q24_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q24_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q24_opt4.jpg"]}}},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000070905","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"Select a figure from amongst the Answer Figures (1, 2, 3, 4) which will continue the same series as established by the five Problem Figures.<br>Problem Figures:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q25.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"उत्तर आकृतियों (1, 2, 3, 4) में से वह आकृति चुनिए जो पाँच समस्या आकृतियों द्वारा स्थापित उसी श्रृंखला को आगे बढ़ाएगी।<br>समस्या आकृतियाँ:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q25.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Observe the movement of the dots and of the arrows from one problem figure to the next:<br>The four dots keep shifting to the next side of the square (top → left → bottom → right …) and the arrows increase in number one by one while turning in the same direction.<br>Continuing this pattern, in the next figure the dots must come on the right side and four arrows must point towards the left — exactly the arrangement shown in answer figure (4).<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 4.</b>","hi":"एक समस्या आकृति से अगली तक बिंदुओं और तीरों की गति को देखिए:<br>चारों बिंदु वर्ग की अगली भुजा पर खिसकते रहते हैं (ऊपर → बाएँ → नीचे → दाएँ …) तथा तीरों की संख्या एक-एक बढ़ती जाती है और वे उसी दिशा में घूमते हैं।<br>इसी पैटर्न को आगे बढ़ाने पर अगली आकृति में बिंदु दाईं ओर होने चाहिए और चार तीर बाईं ओर इंगित करने चाहिए — ठीक वैसी ही व्यवस्था उत्तर आकृति (4) में है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 4 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q25.jpg"]}}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000070906","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Indus Valley Civilization","question":{"en":"Which tiny settlement of the Harappan Civilization was almost exclusively devoted to craft production, including bead-making? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"हड़प्पा सभ्यता की कौन-सी छोटी बस्ती लगभग पूर्णतः शिल्प उत्पादन, जिसमें मनका निर्माण भी शामिल है, के लिए समर्पित थी? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mohenjodaro","hi":"मोहनजोदड़ो"},"2":{"en":"Chanhudaro","hi":"चन्हूदड़ो"},"3":{"en":"Kalibangan","hi":"कालीबंगा"},"4":{"en":"Banawali","hi":"बनवाली"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Chanhudaro</b><br><b>Chanhudaro</b>, a small Harappan settlement in Sindh, was almost exclusively devoted to <b>craft production</b>, including <b>bead-making, shell cutting, seal making and metal work</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Chanhudaro had <b>no citadel</b> and is known as a <b>workshop site</b> with evidence of a bead-making factory and a bronze toy cart.<br>• <b>Lothal</b> in Gujarat was a bead factory and port, while <b>Chanhudaro</b> was primarily a craft centre near Mohenjodaro.<br>• <b>Kalibangan</b> in Rajasthan is known for its <b>ploughed field and fire altars</b>, and <b>Banawali</b> in Haryana for its <b>radial street pattern</b>.<br>• <b>Mohenjodaro</b> was a major city with the <b>Great Bath, granary and Great Bath complex</b>, excavated by R.D. Banerji.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – चन्हूदड़ो</b><br><b>चन्हूदड़ो</b>, सिंध की एक छोटी हड़प्पा बस्ती, लगभग पूर्णतः <b>शिल्प उत्पादन</b> के लिए समर्पित थी, जिसमें <b>मनका निर्माण, शंख कटाई, मुहर निर्माण तथा धातु कार्य</b> शामिल थे।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• चन्हूदड़ो में <b>कोई गढ़ी नहीं</b> थी और यह <b>कार्यशाला स्थल</b> के रूप में जाना जाता है, जहाँ मनका निर्माण कारखाना तथा कांस्य का खिलौना गाड़ी मिली।<br>• गुजरात का <b>लोथल</b> मनका कारखाना तथा बंदरगाह था, जबकि <b>चन्हूदड़ो</b> मोहनजोदड़ो के निकट मुख्यतः शिल्प केंद्र था।<br>• राजस्थान की <b>कालीबंगा</b> <b>जुते हुए खेत तथा अग्नि वेदियों</b> के लिए तथा हरियाणा की <b>बनवाली</b> <b>त्रिज्यीय मार्ग योजना</b> के लिए जानी जाती है।<br>• <b>मोहनजोदड़ो</b> <b>महान स्नानागार, अन्नागार तथा महान स्नान परिसर</b> वाला प्रमुख नगर था, जिसका उत्खनन आर.डी. बनर्जी ने किया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000070907","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: Delhi Sultanate","question":{"en":"During Qutbuddin Aibak's reign, which city served as his administrative capital? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कुतुबुद्दीन ऐबक के शासनकाल में कौन-सा नगर उसकी प्रशासनिक राजधानी था? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ghazni","hi":"गजनी"},"2":{"en":"Lahore","hi":"लाहौर"},"3":{"en":"Delhi","hi":"दिल्ली"},"4":{"en":"Multan","hi":"मुल्तान"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Lahore</b><br><b>Qutbuddin Aibak</b>, the founder of the <b>Mamluk (Slave) dynasty</b>, ruled from <b>1206 to 1210</b> and used <b>Lahore</b> as his administrative capital, though he built extensively in Delhi.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Aibak began the construction of the <b>Qutb Minar</b> in Delhi and built the <b>Quwwat-ul-Islam mosque</b> and the <b>Adhai Din Ka Jhonpra</b> at Ajmer.<br>• <b>Iltutmish</b>, his successor, shifted the capital from Lahore to <b>Delhi</b> and completed the Qutb Minar.<br>• Aibak was known as <b>Lakh Baksh</b> (giver of lakhs) for his generosity and died at Lahore in <b>1210</b>.<br>• His tomb is located at <b>Anarkali, Lahore</b>, and the Slave dynasty ruled until <b>1290</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – लाहौर</b><br><b>गुलाम वंश</b> के संस्थापक <b>कुतुबुद्दीन ऐबक</b> ने <b>1206 से 1210</b> तक शासन किया और <b>लाहौर</b> को अपनी प्रशासनिक राजधानी बनाया, यद्यपि उसने दिल्ली में विस्तार से निर्माण कराया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ऐबक ने दिल्ली में <b>कुतुब मीनार</b> का निर्माण आरंभ किया तथा <b>कुव्वत-उल-इस्लाम मस्जिद</b> एवं अजमेर में <b>अढ़ाई दिन का झोंपड़ा</b> बनवाया।<br>• उसके उत्तराधिकारी <b>इल्तुतमिश</b> ने राजधानी लाहौर से <b>दिल्ली</b> स्थानांतरित की तथा कुतुब मीनार पूरी कराई।<br>• ऐबक अपनी उदारता के कारण <b>लाख बख्श</b> (लाखों का दानी) कहलाया और <b>1210</b> में लाहौर में उसकी मृत्यु हुई।<br>• उसकी समाधि <b>अनारकली, लाहौर</b> में है तथा गुलाम वंश ने <b>1290</b> तक शासन किया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000070908","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Stone Age","question":{"en":"In which modern-day country is the Neolithic site of Mehrgarh located? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"नवपाषाण स्थल मेहरगढ़ आज के किस देश में स्थित है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"India","hi":"भारत"},"2":{"en":"Iran","hi":"ईरान"},"3":{"en":"Pakistan","hi":"पाकिस्तान"},"4":{"en":"Afghanistan","hi":"अफ़ग़ानिस्तान"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Pakistan</b><br><b>Mehrgarh</b> is located in <b>Balochistan province of Pakistan</b>, on the Kachi plain near the Bolan Pass, and is one of the earliest <b>Neolithic farming sites</b> in South Asia.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Mehrgarh dates from about <b>7000 BCE</b> and shows early cultivation of <b>wheat and barley</b> along with domestication of <b>goats and sheep</b>.<br>• Excavations by <b>Jean-François Jarrige</b> revealed <b>mud-brick houses, granaries and burial goods</b> including ornaments.<br>• The site is important for the study of the <b>transition from hunting-gathering to settled agriculture</b> in the subcontinent.<br>• Other Neolithic sites include <b>Burzahom (Kashmir), Chirand (Bihar), Koldihwa (Uttar Pradesh) and Paiyyampalli (Tamil Nadu)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – पाकिस्तान</b><br><b>मेहरगढ़</b> <b>पाकिस्तान के बलोचिस्तान प्रांत</b> में बोलन दर्रे के निकट कच्ची मैदान में स्थित है और दक्षिण एशिया के सबसे प्रारंभिक <b>नवपाषाण कृषि स्थलों</b> में से एक है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मेहरगढ़ लगभग <b>7000 ईसा पूर्व</b> का है और यहाँ <b>गेहूँ तथा जौ</b> की प्रारंभिक खेती तथा <b>बकरी एवं भेड़</b> का पालन के साक्ष्य मिले।<br>• <b>जीन-फ्रांस्वा जारिज</b> के उत्खनन से <b>कच्ची ईंट के घर, अन्नागार तथा आभूषण सहित कब्र सामग्री</b> प्राप्त हुई।<br>• यह स्थल उपमहाद्वीप में <b>शिकार-संग्रह से स्थायी कृषि की ओर संक्रमण</b> के अध्ययन के लिए महत्वपूर्ण है।<br>• अन्य नवपाषाण स्थलों में <b>बुर्जहोम (कश्मीर), चिरांद (बिहार), कोलडिहवा (उत्तर प्रदेश) तथा पैयमपल्ली (तमिलनाडु)</b> शामिल हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000070909","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Dams, Lakes and Waterfall","question":{"en":"In which state is the Idukki Hydroelectric Project, known for its unique double-curvature arch dam, located? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"अपने अनोखे द्वि-वक्रता मेहराब बाँध के लिए प्रसिद्ध इडुक्की जलविद्युत परियोजना किस राज्य में स्थित है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Tamil Nadu","hi":"तमिलनाडु"},"2":{"en":"Kerala","hi":"केरल"},"3":{"en":"Karnataka","hi":"कर्नाटक"},"4":{"en":"Andhra Pradesh","hi":"आंध्र प्रदेश"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Kerala</b><br>The <b>Idukki Hydroelectric Project</b> is located in <b>Idukki district of Kerala</b> and its dam is a <b>double-curvature arch dam</b>, the first of its kind in India.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Idukki arch dam</b>, built across the <b>Periyar river</b> between the Kuravan and Kurathi hills, is one of the <b>highest arch dams in Asia</b>.<br>• The project includes the <b>Cheruthoni and Kulamavu dams</b>, which together form the reservoir.<br>• Hydropower projects in Kerala include <b>Sabarigiri, Sholayar, Idamalayar and Kuttiyadi</b>.<br>• Other famous Indian dams are the <b>Bhakra Nangal (Satluj), Hirakud (Mahanadi), Sardar Sarovar (Narmada) and Nagarjuna Sagar (Krishna)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – केरल</b><br><b>इडुक्की जलविद्युत परियोजना</b> <b>केरल के इडुक्की जिले</b> में स्थित है और इसका बाँध <b>द्वि-वक्रता मेहराब बाँध</b> है, जो भारत में अपनी तरह का पहला है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>इडुक्की मेहराब बाँध</b> कुरवन तथा कुरथी पहाड़ियों के बीच <b>पेरियार नदी</b> पर बना है और <b>एशिया के सबसे ऊँचे मेहराब बाँधों</b> में से एक है।<br>• परियोजना में <b>चेरुथोनी तथा कुलमावु बाँध</b> शामिल हैं, जो मिलकर जलाशय बनाते हैं।<br>• केरल की जलविद्युत परियोजनाओं में <b>सबरीगिरि, शोलायर, इडमलयार तथा कुट्टियाडी</b> शामिल हैं।<br>• भारत के अन्य प्रसिद्ध बाँध <b>भाखड़ा नांगल (सतलुज), हीराकुंड (महानदी), सरदार सरोवर (नर्मदा) तथा नागार्जुन सागर (कृष्णा)</b> हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000070910","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Motion","question":{"en":"Which quantity is calculated by dividing the total distance travelled by the total time interval? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कुल तय दूरी को कुल समय अंतराल से भाग देकर कौन-सी राशि निकाली जाती है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Average speed","hi":"औसत चाल"},"2":{"en":"Average velocity","hi":"औसत वेग"},"3":{"en":"Average acceleration","hi":"औसत त्वरण"},"4":{"en":"Instantaneous speed","hi":"तात्कालिक चाल"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Average speed</b><br><b>Average speed</b> is the <b>total distance travelled divided by the total time interval</b> taken.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Average velocity</b> is total <b>displacement</b> divided by total time, and it can be zero if the object returns to the starting point.<br>• <b>Instantaneous speed</b> is the speed at a particular instant, equal to the slope of the distance-time graph at that point.<br>• <b>Average acceleration</b> is the change in velocity divided by the time interval.<br>• Average speed is a <b>scalar</b> and can never be negative, while average velocity is a <b>vector</b> and can be positive, negative or zero.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – औसत चाल</b><br><b>औसत चाल</b> <b>कुल तय दूरी को लिए गए कुल समय अंतराल</b> से भाग देकर निकाली जाती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>औसत वेग</b> कुल <b>विस्थापन</b> को कुल समय से भाग देकर निकाला जाता है और यदि वस्तु प्रारंभिक बिंदु पर लौट आए तो यह शून्य हो सकता है।<br>• <b>तात्कालिक चाल</b> किसी विशेष क्षण की चाल है, जो उस बिंदु पर दूरी-समय ग्राफ की प्रवणता के बराबर होती है।<br>• <b>औसत त्वरण</b> वेग में परिवर्तन को समय अंतराल से भाग देकर निकाला जाता है।<br>• औसत चाल <b>अदिश</b> राशि है और ऋणात्मक नहीं हो सकती, जबकि औसत वेग <b>सदिश</b> राशि है जो धनात्मक, ऋणात्मक अथवा शून्य हो सकता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000070911","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Minerals","question":{"en":"Which of the following locations in India is known for brown coal (lignite) deposits? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा स्थान भूरे कोयले (लिग्नाइट) के भंडार के लिए जाना जाता है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Neyveli, Tamil Nadu","hi":"नेवेली, तमिलनाडु"},"2":{"en":"Korba, Chhattisgarh","hi":"कोरबा, छत्तीसगढ़"},"3":{"en":"Talcher, Odisha","hi":"तालचेर, ओडिशा"},"4":{"en":"Darangiri, Gujarat","hi":"दारांगिरी, गुजरात"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Neyveli, Tamil Nadu</b><br><b>Neyveli</b> in <b>Tamil Nadu</b> is famous for large deposits of <b>lignite (brown coal)</b>, mined by opencast methods and used in thermal power generation.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Neyveli Lignite Corporation</b> (NLC India) operates the mines and thermal power stations there.<br>• Lignite is a <b>low-grade coal</b> with high moisture and low carbon content, used mainly for power generation and gasification.<br>• Other lignite deposits are found in <b>Gujarat (Kachchh, Bharuch), Rajasthan (Palana) and Jammu and Kashmir</b>.<br>• <b>Korba and Talcher</b> are known for <b>high-grade coal</b>, and the Darangiri area of Gujarat is not a major coal field.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – नेवेली, तमिलनाडु</b><br><b>तमिलनाडु</b> का <b>नेवेली</b> <b>लिग्नाइट (भूरे कोयले)</b> के विशाल भंडार के लिए प्रसिद्ध है, जिसका खनन खुली खदान से होता है और ताप विद्युत उत्पादन में उपयोग होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• वहाँ <b>नेवेली लिग्नाइट निगम</b> (NLC इंडिया) खदानें तथा ताप विद्युत केंद्र संचालित करता है।<br>• लिग्नाइट <b>निम्न श्रेणी का कोयला</b> है जिसमें अधिक नमी तथा कम कार्बन होता है; यह मुख्यतः विद्युत उत्पादन तथा गैसीकरण में प्रयुक्त होता है।<br>• अन्य लिग्नाइट भंडार <b>गुजरात (कच्छ, भरूच), राजस्थान (पलाना) तथा जम्मू-कश्मीर</b> में मिलते हैं।<br>• <b>कोरबा तथा तालचेर</b> <b>उच्च श्रेणी के कोयले</b> के लिए जाने जाते हैं, तथा गुजरात का दारांगिरी क्षेत्र प्रमुख कोयला क्षेत्र नहीं है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000070912","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"In which Indian state is the traditional festival of Pang-Lhabsol associated? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"पांग-ल्हाबसोल पारंपरिक उत्सव किस भारतीय राज्य से संबंधित है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Nagaland","hi":"नगालैंड"},"2":{"en":"Sikkim","hi":"सिक्किम"},"3":{"en":"Assam","hi":"असम"},"4":{"en":"Mizoram","hi":"मिजोरम"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Sikkim</b><br><b>Pang-Lhabsol</b> is a festival of <b>Sikkim</b>, celebrated mainly by the <b>Bhutia and Lepcha</b> communities to honour the local deity <b>Mount Khangchendzonga</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The festival is held in the <b>Lepcha month of Khempu</b>, usually in August-September, and features masked dances and the <b>Pang Toed Chaam</b>.<br>• It is associated with the <b>guardian deity of Sikkim</b> and is also celebrated by the Indian Army at <b>Gan-gan in North Sikkim</b>.<br>• Other Sikkim festivals are <b>Losar, Saga Dawa, Drukpa Tseshi, Losoong and Tihar</b>.<br>• Nagaland is known for the <b>Hornbill Festival</b>, Assam for <b>Bihu</b> and Mizoram for <b>Chapchar Kut</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सिक्किम</b><br><b>पांग-ल्हाबसोल</b> <b>सिक्किम</b> का उत्सव है, जो मुख्यतः <b>भूटिया तथा लेपचा</b> समुदायों द्वारा स्थानीय देवता <b>माउंट कंचनजंगा</b> के सम्मान में मनाया जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह उत्सव <b>लेपचा मास खेम्पू</b> में, सामान्यतः अगस्त-सितंबर में होता है और इसमें मुखौटा नृत्य तथा <b>पांग तोएद चाम</b> प्रस्तुत होता है।<br>• यह <b>सिक्किम के रक्षक देवता</b> से संबंधित है और भारतीय सेना द्वारा <b>उत्तरी सिक्किम के गान-गान</b> में भी मनाया जाता है।<br>• सिक्किम के अन्य उत्सव <b>लोसार, सागा दावा, द्रुक्पा त्सेशी, लोसूंग तथा तिहार</b> हैं।<br>• नगालैंड <b>हॉर्नबिल महोत्सव</b>, असम <b>बिहू</b> तथा मिजोरम <b>चापचर कुट</b> के लिए जाना जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000070913","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"In July 2025, Parag Jain assumed charge as the head of which external intelligence agency of India? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"जुलाई 2025 में पाराग जैन ने भारत की किस बाह्य गुप्तचर एजेंसी के प्रमुख का पदभार संभाला? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Intelligence Bureau (IB)","hi":"आसूचना ब्यूरो (IB)"},"2":{"en":"Research and Analysis Wing (R&AW)","hi":"अनुसंधान तथा विश्लेषण विंग (R&AW)"},"3":{"en":"Defense Intelligence Agency (DIA)","hi":"रक्षा आसूचना एजेंसी (DIA)"},"4":{"en":"National Technical Research Organisation (NTRO)","hi":"राष्ट्रीय तकनीकी अनुसंधान संगठन (NTRO)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Research and Analysis Wing (R&AW)</b><br>In <b>July 2025</b>, <b>Parag Jain</b> assumed charge as the <b>Secretary, Research and Analysis Wing (R&AW)</b>, India's external intelligence agency.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>R&AW</b> was created in <b>1968</b>, largely on the initiative of <b>R.N. Kao</b>, its first chief, after intelligence gaps in the 1962 and 1965 wars.<br>• R&AW collects <b>external intelligence</b> and operates under the <b>Cabinet Secretariat</b>, and its chief is designated Secretary (R).<br>• The <b>Intelligence Bureau</b> handles internal intelligence, and the <b>NTRO</b> deals with technical intelligence.<br>• <b>Parag Jain</b> is a senior officer who has earlier served in the R&AW and in other intelligence-related assignments.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – अनुसंधान तथा विश्लेषण विंग (R&AW)</b><br><b>जुलाई 2025</b> में <b>पाराग जैन</b> ने भारत की बाह्य गुप्तचर एजेंसी <b>अनुसंधान तथा विश्लेषण विंग (R&AW)</b> के <b>सचिव</b> का पदभार संभाला।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>R&AW</b> की स्थापना <b>1968</b> में हुई, मुख्यतः इसके प्रथम प्रमुख <b>आर.एन. काव</b> की पहल पर, 1962 तथा 1965 के युद्धों में आसूचना संबंधी कमियों के बाद।<br>• R&AW <b>बाह्य आसूचना</b> एकत्र करता है और <b>मंत्रिमंडल सचिवालय</b> के अधीन कार्य करता है; इसके प्रमुख को सचिव (R) कहा जाता है।<br>• <b>आसूचना ब्यूरो</b> आंतरिक आसूचना देखता है तथा <b>NTRO</b> तकनीकी आसूचना से संबंधित है।<br>• <b>पाराग जैन</b> वरिष्ठ अधिकारी हैं जिन्होंने पहले R&AW तथा अन्य आसूचना संबंधी पदों पर सेवा की है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000070914","section":"GK","topic":"Science and Technology: Science and Technology","question":{"en":"Dr. V. Narayanan, former Director of ISRO's (Indian Space Research Organisation) Liquid Propulsion Systems Centre, played a key role in which major space technology achievement? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"इसरो (भारतीय अंतरिक्ष अनुसंधान संगठन) के द्रव प्रणोदन प्रणाली केंद्र के पूर्व निदेशक डॉ. वी. नारायणन ने किस प्रमुख अंतरिक्ष तकनीक उपलब्धि में महत्वपूर्ण भूमिका निभाई? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Launching Mangalyaan-2","hi":"मंगलयान-2 का प्रक्षेपण"},"2":{"en":"Developing the CE-20 cryogenic engine for heavy rockets","hi":"भारी रॉकेटों के लिए CE-20 क्रायोजेनिक इंजन का विकास"},"3":{"en":"Designing the LUPEX (LUnar Polar Exploration) rover","hi":"LUPEX (चंद्र ध्रुवीय अन्वेषण) रोवर का डिज़ाइन"},"4":{"en":"Headlining the Gaganyaan parachute tests","hi":"गगनयान पैराशूट परीक्षणों का नेतृत्व"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Developing the CE-20 cryogenic engine for heavy rockets</b><br>Dr. <b>V. Narayanan</b>, former Director of the <b>Liquid Propulsion Systems Centre</b>, played a key role in developing the <b>CE-20 cryogenic engine</b> that powers the upper stage of the <b>LVM3</b> rocket.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>CE-20</b> is India's first <b>indigenously developed cryogenic engine</b> for heavy launch vehicles, using <b>liquid hydrogen and liquid oxygen</b>.<br>• The <b>LVM3</b> with the CE-20 upper stage carried the <b>Chandrayaan-2 and Chandrayaan-3</b> missions and the <b>OneWeb</b> satellites.<br>• Cryogenic engines give <b>high specific impulse</b>, enabling heavier payloads to geostationary transfer orbit.<br>• Dr. V. Narayanan later became <b>Chairman of ISRO</b> and is known for his work on <b>liquid propulsion and cryogenic technology</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – भारी रॉकेटों के लिए CE-20 क्रायोजेनिक इंजन का विकास</b><br><b>द्रव प्रणोदन प्रणाली केंद्र</b> के पूर्व निदेशक डॉ. <b>वी. नारायणन</b> ने <b>CE-20 क्रायोजेनिक इंजन</b> के विकास में महत्वपूर्ण भूमिका निभाई, जो <b>LVM3</b> रॉकेट के ऊपरी चरण को शक्ति देता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>CE-20</b> भारी प्रक्षेपण यानों के लिए भारत का पहला <b>स्वदेशी क्रायोजेनिक इंजन</b> है, जिसमें <b>द्रव हाइड्रोजन तथा द्रव ऑक्सीजन</b> का उपयोग होता है।<br>• CE-20 ऊपरी चरण वाले <b>LVM3</b> ने <b>चंद्रयान-2 तथा चंद्रयान-3</b> मिशन तथा <b>वनवेब</b> उपग्रह प्रक्षेपित किए।<br>• क्रायोजेनिक इंजन <b>उच्च विशिष्ट आवेग</b> देते हैं, जिससे भूस्थैतिक अंतरण कक्षा में अधिक भार ले जाना संभव होता है।<br>• डॉ. वी. नारायणन बाद में <b>इसरो के अध्यक्ष</b> बने और <b>द्रव प्रणोदन तथा क्रायोजेनिक तकनीक</b> में अपने कार्य के लिए जाने जाते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000070915","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Atmosphere","question":{"en":"Consider the following statements about the troposphere:<br>1. The troposphere is called the \"changing sphere\" because air in this layer is always in motion.<br>2. The temperature in the troposphere decreases with height at a rate of about 1 degree Celsius per 265 metres, known as the Fast lapse rate.<br>Which of the statements above is/are <b>correct</b>? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"क्षोभमंडल के बारे में निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार करें:<br>1. क्षोभमंडल को \"परिवर्तनशील मंडल\" कहा जाता है क्योंकि इस परत की वायु सदैव गतिमान रहती है।<br>2. क्षोभमंडल में ऊँचाई के साथ तापमान लगभग 265 मीटर प्रति 1 डिग्री सेल्सियस की दर से घटता है, जिसे फास्ट लैप्स रेट कहते हैं।<br>उपर्युक्त कथनों में से कौन-सा/से <b>सही</b> है/हैं? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 only","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"2 only","hi":"केवल 2"},"3":{"en":"Both 1 and 2 are correct","hi":"1 तथा 2 दोनों सही हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither 1 nor 2 is correct","hi":"न 1 और न 2 सही हैं"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – 1 only</b><br>Statement 1 is correct because the <b>troposphere</b> is called the <b>changing sphere</b> as its air is always in motion, producing weather. Statement 2 is wrong because the normal lapse rate is about <b>1 degree Celsius per 165 metres</b>, and the term \"Fast lapse rate\" is not the standard name for it.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The troposphere is the <b>lowest layer</b> of the atmosphere, extending up to about <b>8 km at the poles and 18 km at the equator</b>.<br>• It contains most of the atmosphere's <b>water vapour, dust and clouds</b> and is where all <b>weather phenomena</b> occur.<br>• The <b>normal lapse rate</b> of temperature is about <b>6.5 degrees Celsius per kilometre</b> of ascent, that is 1 degree Celsius per 165 metres.<br>• The boundary between the troposphere and the stratosphere is the <b>tropopause</b>, where temperature stops falling with height.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – केवल 1</b><br>कथन 1 सही है क्योंकि <b>क्षोभमंडल</b> को <b>परिवर्तनशील मंडल</b> कहा जाता है, क्योंकि इसकी वायु सदैव गतिमान रहती है और मौसम उत्पन्न करती है। कथन 2 गलत है क्योंकि सामान्य ताप-ह्रास दर लगभग <b>165 मीटर प्रति 1 डिग्री सेल्सियस</b> है तथा \"फास्ट लैप्स रेट\" इसका मानक नाम नहीं है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• क्षोभमंडल वायुमंडल की <b>सबसे निचली परत</b> है, जो ध्रुवों पर लगभग <b>8 किमी तथा विषुवत रेखा पर 18 किमी</b> तक फैली है।<br>• इसमें वायुमंडल का अधिकांश <b>जलवाष्प, धूल तथा बादल</b> होते हैं और सभी <b>मौसम संबंधी घटनाएँ</b> यहीं होती हैं।<br>• तापमान की <b>सामान्य ह्रास दर</b> प्रति किलोमीटर ऊँचाई पर लगभग <b>6.5 डिग्री सेल्सियस</b> है, अर्थात 165 मीटर पर 1 डिग्री सेल्सियस।<br>• क्षोभमंडल तथा समतापमंडल के बीच की सीमा <b>क्षोभसीमा</b> है, जहाँ ऊँचाई के साथ तापमान गिरना रुक जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000070916","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"The Prime Minister's Development Initiative for North East Region (PM-DevINE) in India is fully funded by which organization? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत में पूर्वोत्तर क्षेत्र के लिए प्रधानमंत्री की विकास पहल (PM-DevINE) किस संगठन द्वारा पूर्णतः वित्तपोषित है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Reserve Bank of India","hi":"भारतीय रिज़र्व बैंक"},"2":{"en":"Government of India","hi":"भारत सरकार"},"3":{"en":"National Development Council (NDC), India","hi":"राष्ट्रीय विकास परिषद (NDC), भारत"},"4":{"en":"NITI Aayog, India","hi":"नीति आयोग, भारत"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Government of India</b><br><b>PM-DevINE</b> is <b>fully funded by the Government of India</b> through the <b>Ministry of Development of North Eastern Region (DoNER)</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The scheme was announced in the Union Budget <b>2022-23</b> with an outlay of about <b>6,600 crore rupees</b> for the period up to 2025-26.<br>• It supports <b>infrastructure, social development and livelihood projects</b> in the eight north-eastern states, chosen for their potential to create <b>sustainable employment</b>.<br>• It complements other schemes such as the <b>North East Special Infrastructure Development Scheme (NESIDS)</b> and the <b>North East Council</b> programmes.<br>• The Ministry of DoNER coordinates the development of the region, which includes the <b>eight states of the North East</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – भारत सरकार</b><br><b>PM-DevINE</b> को <b>भारत सरकार</b> <b>पूर्वोत्तर क्षेत्र विकास मंत्रालय (DoNER)</b> के माध्यम से <b>पूर्णतः वित्तपोषित</b> करती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• योजना की घोषणा केंद्रीय बजट <b>2022-23</b> में हुई और इसका परिव्यय 2025-26 तक लगभग <b>6,600 करोड़ रुपये</b> है।<br>• यह आठ पूर्वोत्तर राज्यों में <b>अवसंरचना, सामाजिक विकास तथा आजीविका परियोजनाओं</b> को सहायता देती है, जिन्हें <b>सतत रोजगार</b> सृजन की क्षमता के आधार पर चुना जाता है।<br>• यह <b>पूर्वोत्तर विशेष अवसंरचना विकास योजना (NESIDS)</b> तथा <b>पूर्वोत्तर परिषद</b> के कार्यक्रमों जैसी योजनाओं का पूरक है।<br>• DoNER मंत्रालय क्षेत्र के विकास का समन्वय करता है, जिसमें <b>पूर्वोत्तर के आठ राज्य</b> सम्मिलित हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000070917","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Awards and Honours (Current)","question":{"en":"Which Hindi memoir won the Sahitya Akademi Award 2025? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कौन-सी हिंदी संस्मरण-कृति साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार 2025 प्राप्त किया? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Karhi Khelar Sadhu","hi":"कढ़ी खेलर साधु"},"2":{"en":"Jeete Jee Allahabad","hi":"जीते जी इलाहाबाद"},"3":{"en":"Dada Seerisu Tande","hi":"दादा सीरिसु तांदे"},"4":{"en":"Safar Jaari Hai","hi":"सफ़र जारी है"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Jeete Jee Allahabad</b><br><b>Jeete Jee Allahabad</b> is a <b>Hindi memoir</b> that won the <b>Sahitya Akademi Award 2025</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Sahitya Akademi Award</b> is given annually for outstanding literary work in each recognised language and carries a <b>plaque, a casket and a cash prize of 1 lakh rupees</b>.<br>• The award is conferred by the <b>Sahitya Akademi</b>, India's national academy of letters, established in <b>1954</b>.<br>• <b>Memoirs and travelogues</b> are among the recognised categories, along with poetry, novels, short stories and literary criticism.<br>• The highest literary honour in India is the <b>Jnanpith Award</b>, while the Sahitya Akademi also gives <b>translation prizes and Yuva Puraskar</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – जीते जी इलाहाबाद</b><br><b>जीते जी इलाहाबाद</b> एक <b>हिंदी संस्मरण</b> है, जिसने <b>साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार 2025</b> प्राप्त किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार</b> प्रत्येक वर्ष प्रत्येक मान्य भाषा में उत्कृष्ट साहित्यिक कृति पर दिया जाता है और इसमें <b>ताम्रपत्र, पत्रिका तथा 1 लाख रुपये की नकद राशि</b> मिलती है।<br>• यह पुरस्कार <b>साहित्य अकादमी</b> देती है, जो भारत की राष्ट्रीय साहित्य अकादमी है और <b>1954</b> में स्थापित हुई।<br>• <b>संस्मरण तथा यात्रा-वृत्तांत</b> मान्य श्रेणियों में हैं, साथ में कविता, उपन्यास, कहानी तथा साहित्यिक आलोचना भी।<br>• भारत का सर्वोच्च साहित्यिक सम्मान <b>ज्ञानपीठ पुरस्कार</b> है, तथा साहित्य अकादमी <b>अनुवाद पुरस्कार तथा युवा पुरस्कार</b> भी देती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000070918","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Himalayas","question":{"en":"What type of geographical unit are the Northern Plains and the Himalayas considered to be? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"उत्तरी मैदान तथा हिमालय किस प्रकार की भौगोलिक इकाई माने जाते हैं? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Volcanic landforms","hi":"ज्वालामुखी स्थलाकृतियाँ"},"2":{"en":"Most recent landforms","hi":"सर्वाधिक नवीन स्थलाकृतियाँ"},"3":{"en":"Oldest landforms of India","hi":"भारत की सबसे प्राचीन स्थलाकृतियाँ"},"4":{"en":"Most stable landforms","hi":"सर्वाधिक स्थिर स्थलाकृतियाँ"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Most recent landforms</b><br>The <b>Himalayas</b> and the <b>Northern Plains</b> are among the <b>most recent landforms</b> of the Indian subcontinent, formed by the collision of the Indian and Eurasian plates and by the deposition of alluvium.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Himalayas are <b>young fold mountains</b> and are still rising, making the region <b>seismically active</b>.<br>• The <b>Northern Plains</b> are formed of <b>alluvium</b> brought by the Indus, Ganga and Brahmaputra rivers and are among the most fertile regions.<br>• The <b>Peninsular Plateau</b>, by contrast, is one of the <b>oldest and most stable landforms</b>, part of the Gondwana shield.<br>• The Himalayas act as a <b>climatic barrier</b>, block the cold Central Asian winds and force the monsoon to shed rain over the plains.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सर्वाधिक नवीन स्थलाकृतियाँ</b><br><b>हिमालय</b> तथा <b>उत्तरी मैदान</b> भारतीय उपमहाद्वीप की <b>सर्वाधिक नवीन स्थलाकृतियों</b> में हैं, जो भारतीय तथा यूरेशियन प्लेटों के टकराव तथा जलोढ़ निक्षेपण से बनीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• हिमालय <b>नवीन वलित पर्वत</b> हैं और अभी भी ऊँचे उठ रहे हैं, जिससे यह क्षेत्र <b>भूकंपीय दृष्टि से सक्रिय</b> है।<br>• <b>उत्तरी मैदान</b> सिंधु, गंगा तथा ब्रह्मपुत्र नदियों द्वारा लाए <b>जलोढ़</b> से बने हैं और अत्यंत उपजाऊ क्षेत्रों में हैं।<br>• इसके विपरीत <b>प्रायद्वीपीय पठार</b> <b>सबसे प्राचीन तथा स्थिर स्थलाकृतियों</b> में है और गोंडवाना शिल्ड का भाग है।<br>• हिमालय <b>जलवायु अवरोध</b> का कार्य करता है, मध्य एशिया की ठंडी हवाओं को रोकता है तथा मानसून को मैदानों पर वर्षा के लिए विवश करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000070919","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"A judicial magistrate's local jurisdiction extends partly into another district where he does not ordinarily hold court. A legal provision refers to \"the Court of Session having jurisdiction\". How should this expression be interpreted under the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 in India? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक न्यायिक मजिस्ट्रेट का स्थानीय क्षेत्राधिकार आंशिक रूप से ऐसे अन्य जिले में फैला है जहाँ वह सामान्यतः न्यायालय नहीं रखता। एक विधिक प्रावधान \"क्षेत्राधिकार रखने वाले सत्र न्यायालय\" का उल्लेख करता है। भारत में भारतीय नागरिक सुरक्षा संहिता, 2023 के अंतर्गत इस अभिव्यक्ति की व्याख्या कैसे की जानी चाहिए? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It refers only to the sessions court where the magistrate physically sits.","hi":"यह केवल उस सत्र न्यायालय को दर्शाता है जहाँ मजिस्ट्रेट भौतिक रूप से बैठता है।"},"2":{"en":"It refers to the Sessions Court exercising jurisdiction over the concerned area.","hi":"यह संबंधित क्षेत्र पर क्षेत्राधिकार का प्रयोग करने वाले सत्र न्यायालय को दर्शाता है।"},"3":{"en":"It automatically refers to the High Court.","hi":"यह स्वतः उच्च न्यायालय को दर्शाता है।"},"4":{"en":"It refers to any sessions court chosen by the state government.","hi":"यह राज्य सरकार द्वारा चुने गए किसी भी सत्र न्यायालय को दर्शाता है।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – It refers to the Sessions Court exercising jurisdiction over the concerned area</b><br>Under the <b>BNSS, 2023</b>, where a magistrate exercises jurisdiction over an area partly in another district, the expression \"the Court of Session having jurisdiction\" refers to the <b>Sessions Court that exercises jurisdiction over that concerned area</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The provision avoids a situation where a case would fail only because the magistrate does not ordinarily sit in the district in which part of his jurisdiction lies.<br>• Jurisdiction is determined by the <b>territorial limits of the court</b>, not by the place where the magistrate happens to sit.<br>• The <b>Sessions Court</b> is headed by a <b>Sessions Judge</b> and tries serious offences, and appeals from magistrates lie to it.<br>• The BNSS replaced the <b>Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973</b> and came into force on <b>1 July 2024</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – यह संबंधित क्षेत्र पर क्षेत्राधिकार का प्रयोग करने वाले सत्र न्यायालय को दर्शाता है।</b><br><b>BNSS, 2023</b> के अंतर्गत जहाँ मजिस्ट्रेट का क्षेत्राधिकार आंशिक रूप से अन्य जिले में है, वहाँ \"क्षेत्राधिकार रखने वाले सत्र न्यायालय\" का अर्थ <b>उस संबंधित क्षेत्र पर क्षेत्राधिकार का प्रयोग करने वाला सत्र न्यायालय</b> है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह प्रावधान ऐसी स्थिति से बचाता है जहाँ कोई मामला केवल इस कारण विफल हो जाए कि मजिस्ट्रेट सामान्यतः उस जिले में नहीं बैठता जिसमें उसके क्षेत्राधिकार का भाग है।<br>• क्षेत्राधिकार <b>न्यायालय की भौगोलिक सीमाओं</b> से निर्धारित होता है, न कि उस स्थान से जहाँ मजिस्ट्रेट संयोगवश बैठता है।<br>• <b>सत्र न्यायालय</b> का प्रमुख <b>सत्र न्यायाधीश</b> होता है, जो गंभीर अपराधों का विचारण करता है तथा मजिस्ट्रेटों के निर्णयों की अपील उसी में होती है।<br>• BNSS ने <b>दंड प्रक्रिया संहिता, 1973</b> का स्थान लिया और यह <b>1 जुलाई 2024</b> से प्रभावी हुई।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000070920","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"At just 13 years old, who became the youngest girl in the world to scale Mount Everest and later also scaled Mount Elbrus? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"मात्र 13 वर्ष की आयु में कौन विश्व की सबसे युवा लड़की बनी जिसने माउंट एवरेस्ट पर चढ़ाई की और बाद में माउंट एल्ब्रुस पर भी चढ़ाई की? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Kaamya Karthikeyan","hi":"काम्या कार्तिकेयन"},"2":{"en":"Malavath Poorna","hi":"मालावथ पूर्णा"},"3":{"en":"Arunima Sinha","hi":"अरुणिमा सिन्हा"},"4":{"en":"Bachendri Pal","hi":"बछेंद्री पाल"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Malavath Poorna</b><br><b>Malavath Poorna</b>, a tribal girl from <b>Telangana</b>, became the <b>youngest girl in the world to climb Mount Everest</b> at the age of <b>13</b> in <b>2014</b>, and later climbed <b>Mount Elbrus</b>, the highest peak in Europe.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• She was born in a poor family in <b>Nizamabad district</b> and was trained by the <b>Bhongir Mountaineering Society</b> and the Andhra Pradesh government's social welfare programme.<br>• She has also climbed <b>Mount Kilimanjaro, Mount Kosciuszko and Mount Aconcagua</b>, aiming to complete the seven summits.<br>• <b>Bachendri Pal</b> was the <b>first Indian woman</b> to climb Mount Everest, in <b>1984</b>.<br>• <b>Arunima Sinha</b> was the first woman amputee to climb Everest, and <b>Kaamya Karthikeyan</b> climbed Everest as a teenager and completed the seven summits.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – मालावथ पूर्णा</b><br><b>तेलंगाना</b> की आदिवासी बालिका <b>मालावथ पूर्णा</b> <b>2014</b> में <b>13</b> वर्ष की आयु में <b>माउंट एवरेस्ट पर चढ़ने वाली विश्व की सबसे युवा लड़की</b> बनी और बाद में यूरोप की सर्वोच्च चोटी <b>माउंट एल्ब्रुस</b> पर भी चढ़ाई की।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उनका जन्म <b>निजामाबाद जिले</b> के एक निर्धन परिवार में हुआ और प्रशिक्षण <b>भोंगीर पर्वतारोहण समिति</b> तथा आंध्र प्रदेश सरकार के समाज कल्याण कार्यक्रम से मिला।<br>• उन्होंने <b>माउंट किलिमंजारो, माउंट कोसियुस्को तथा माउंट एकोनकागुआ</b> पर भी चढ़ाई की और सात शिखरों को पूरा करने का लक्ष्य रखा है।<br>• <b>बछेंद्री पाल</b> <b>1984</b> में माउंट एवरेस्ट पर चढ़ने वाली <b>पहली भारतीय महिला</b> थीं।<br>• <b>अरुणिमा सिन्हा</b> एवरेस्ट पर चढ़ने वाली पहली दिव्यांग महिला थीं, तथा <b>काम्या कार्तिकेयन</b> ने किशोरी के रूप में एवरेस्ट पर चढ़कर सात शिखर पूरे किए।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000070921","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Awards and Honours (Current)","question":{"en":"Which Indian violin virtuoso was honored with the Padma Vibhushan in the 2025 Republic Day honors? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"2025 के गणतंत्र दिवस सम्मानों में किस भारतीय वायलिन वादक को पद्म विभूषण से सम्मानित किया गया? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Vyjayanthimala Bali","hi":"वैजयंतीमाला बाली"},"2":{"en":"L. Subramaniam","hi":"एल. सुब्रह्मण्यम"},"3":{"en":"Vishwa Mohan Bhatt","hi":"विश्व मोहन भट्ट"},"4":{"en":"Amjad Ali Khan","hi":"अमजद अली खान"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – L. Subramaniam</b><br>The violinist <b>L. Subramaniam</b> was honoured with the <b>Padma Vibhushan in the 2025 Republic Day honours</b> for his contribution to Indian classical music.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>L. Subramaniam</b> is a renowned <b>Carnatic violinist, composer and conductor</b> known for blending Indian classical music with Western and jazz traditions.<br>• He has collaborated with artists such as <b>Yehudi Menuhin, Stephane Grappelli and Herbie Hancock</b> and founded the <b>Lakshminarayana Global Music Festival</b>.<br>• <b>Vyjayanthimala Bali</b> is a dancer and actress, <b>Vishwa Mohan Bhatt</b> is a Mohan veena player, and <b>Amjad Ali Khan</b> is a sarod maestro.<br>• The <b>Padma Vibhushan</b> is the <b>second-highest civilian award</b> of India, after the Bharat Ratna.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – एल. सुब्रह्मण्यम</b><br>वायलिन वादक <b>एल. सुब्रह्मण्यम</b> को भारतीय शास्त्रीय संगीत में योगदान के लिए <b>2025 के गणतंत्र दिवस सम्मानों में पद्म विभूषण</b> से सम्मानित किया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>एल. सुब्रह्मण्यम</b> प्रसिद्ध <b>कर्नाटक वायलिन वादक, संगीतकार तथा संचालक</b> हैं, जो भारतीय शास्त्रीय संगीत को पाश्चात्य तथा जैज़ परंपराओं से जोड़ने के लिए जाने जाते हैं।<br>• उन्होंने <b>यहूदी मेनुहिन, स्टेफेन ग्रापेली तथा हर्बी हैनकॉक</b> जैसे कलाकारों के साथ सहयोग किया और <b>लक्ष्मीनारायण वैश्विक संगीत महोत्सव</b> की स्थापना की।<br>• <b>वैजयंतीमाला बाली</b> नृत्यांगना एवं अभिनेत्री हैं, <b>विश्व मोहन भट्ट</b> मोहन वीणा वादक तथा <b>अमजद अली खान</b> सरोद वादक हैं।<br>• <b>पद्म विभूषण</b> भारत का <b>दूसरा सर्वोच्च नागरिक सम्मान</b> है, भारत रत्न के बाद।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000070922","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: South Indian History & Tripartite Struggle and Cholas","question":{"en":"Which physical characteristic best defines the human figures depicted in the Amaravati school of art? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"अमरावती कला शैली में चित्रित मानव आकृतियों की सर्वोत्तम विशेषता कौन-सी है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Tall, slender bodies","hi":"लंबे, पतले शरीर"},"2":{"en":"Short, bulky builds","hi":"छोटे, भारी शरीर"},"3":{"en":"Extremely muscular physiques","hi":"अत्यधिक पेशीय शरीर"},"4":{"en":"Proportionately oversized heads","hi":"अनुपात से अधिक बड़े सिर"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Tall, slender bodies</b><br>The <b>Amaravati school</b> of art, which flourished in the <b>Satavahana period</b> in the Krishna valley, is known for its <b>tall, slender human figures</b> with graceful, flowing forms.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The school produced <b>sculpture in white marble</b>, mainly for Buddhist stupas, and is famous for the <b>Amaravati Stupa</b> and the panels at <b>Nagarjunakonda</b>.<br>• Figures show <b>naturalistic poses, dynamic movement and fine drapery</b>, unlike the heavier, muscular forms of Mathura art.<br>• The <b>Amaravati Stupa</b>, also called the <b>Mahachaitya</b>, was built by the Satavahanas and later embellished by the <b>Ikshvakus</b>.<br>• The three great schools of early Indian sculpture were <b>Gandhara, Mathura and Amaravati</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – लंबे, पतले शरीर</b><br><b>अमरावती शैली</b>, जो कृष्णा घाटी में <b>सातवाहन काल</b> में फली-फूली, अपनी <b>लंबी, पतली मानव आकृतियों</b> तथा सुडौल लचीली बनावट के लिए जानी जाती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इस शैली में मुख्यतः बौद्ध स्तूपों के लिए <b>श्वेत संगमरमर की मूर्तिकला</b> बनी और यह <b>अमरावती स्तूप</b> तथा <b>नागार्जुनकोंडा</b> के पट्टों के लिए प्रसिद्ध है।<br>• आकृतियों में <b>स्वाभाविक मुद्राएँ, गतिशीलता तथा सूक्ष्म वस्त्राभरण</b> दिखते हैं, जो मथुरा कला के भारी, पेशीय रूपों से भिन्न हैं।<br>• <b>अमरावती स्तूप</b>, जिसे <b>महाचैत्य</b> भी कहते हैं, सातवाहनों ने बनवाया और बाद में <b>इक्ष्वाकुओं</b> ने इसे अलंकृत किया।<br>• प्रारंभिक भारतीय मूर्तिकला की तीन प्रमुख शैलियाँ <b>गांधार, मथुरा तथा अमरावती</b> थीं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000070923","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"The International Cricket Council (ICC) Women's Cricket World Cup 2025 was scheduled to be held during which period? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"अंतर्राष्ट्रीय क्रिकेट परिषद (ICC) महिला क्रिकेट विश्व कप 2025 किस अवधि में आयोजित होना निर्धारित था? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"25 September - 31 October 2025","hi":"25 सितंबर - 31 अक्टूबर 2025"},"2":{"en":"30 September - 2 November 2025","hi":"30 सितंबर - 2 नवंबर 2025"},"3":{"en":"1 October - 5 November 2025","hi":"1 अक्टूबर - 5 नवंबर 2025"},"4":{"en":"5 October - 10 November 2025","hi":"5 अक्टूबर - 10 नवंबर 2025"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – 30 September - 2 November 2025</b><br>The <b>ICC Women's Cricket World Cup 2025</b> was scheduled from <b>30 September to 2 November 2025</b> and was hosted jointly by <b>India and Sri Lanka</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It was the <b>10th edition</b> of the Women's Cricket World Cup, with <b>eight teams</b> competing.<br>• <b>India</b> won the title, defeating <b>South Africa</b> in the final at the <b>DY Patil Stadium, Navi Mumbai</b>, under <b>Harmanpreet Kaur</b>.<br>• The tournament was played in the <b>One Day International</b> format, and <b>Australia</b> is the most successful team in its history.<br>• The first Women's World Cup was held in <b>1973 in England</b>, two years before the men's World Cup.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – 30 सितंबर - 2 नवंबर 2025</b><br><b>ICC महिला क्रिकेट विश्व कप 2025</b> <b>30 सितंबर से 2 नवंबर 2025</b> तक निर्धारित था और इसकी मेजबानी <b>भारत तथा श्रीलंका</b> ने संयुक्त रूप से की।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह महिला क्रिकेट विश्व कप का <b>10वाँ संस्करण</b> था, जिसमें <b>आठ टीमों</b> ने भाग लिया।<br>• <b>भारत</b> ने <b>हरमनप्रीत कौर</b> की कप्तानी में <b>डीवाई पाटिल स्टेडियम, नवी मुंबई</b> में फाइनल में <b>दक्षिण अफ्रीका</b> को हराकर खिताब जीता।<br>• प्रतियोगिता <b>एकदिवसीय अंतर्राष्ट्रीय</b> प्रारूप में खेली गई, तथा इसके इतिहास में <b>ऑस्ट्रेलिया</b> सबसे सफल टीम है।<br>• पहला महिला विश्व कप <b>1973 में इंग्लैंड</b> में हुआ, जो पुरुष विश्व कप से दो वर्ष पहले था।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000070924","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"The 2025 Men's Federation Internationale de Hockey (FIH) Hockey Junior World Cup, hosted by India, started on 28 November 2025 in which state? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत द्वारा आयोजित 2025 पुरुष अंतर्राष्ट्रीय हॉकी महासंघ (FIH) हॉकी जूनियर विश्व कप 28 नवंबर 2025 को किस राज्य में शुरू हुआ? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Odisha","hi":"ओडिशा"},"2":{"en":"Tamil Nadu","hi":"तमिलनाडु"},"3":{"en":"Bihar","hi":"बिहार"},"4":{"en":"Uttar Pradesh","hi":"उत्तर प्रदेश"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Tamil Nadu</b><br>The <b>2025 FIH Hockey Junior World Cup</b> hosted by India began on <b>28 November 2025</b> in <b>Tamil Nadu</b>, with matches played in <b>Chennai</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Junior World Cup</b> is organised by the <b>International Hockey Federation (FIH)</b> for men's teams under 21 years of age.<br>• India has won the men's junior title <b>twice</b>, in <b>2001 and 2016</b>, and hosted the event in <b>2021 in Bhubaneswar</b>.<br>• <b>Tamil Nadu</b> has a strong hockey tradition, with players such as <b>Dhanraj Pillay</b> and the <b>Mayor Radhakrishnan Stadium</b> in Chennai as a major venue.<br>• India's senior men's team won <b>bronze at the Tokyo 2020 Olympics</b> and <b>bronze at the Paris 2024 Olympics</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – तमिलनाडु</b><br>भारत द्वारा आयोजित <b>2025 FIH हॉकी जूनियर विश्व कप</b> <b>28 नवंबर 2025</b> को <b>तमिलनाडु</b> में आरंभ हुआ और मुकाबले <b>चेन्नई</b> में खेले गए।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>जूनियर विश्व कप</b> <b>अंतर्राष्ट्रीय हॉकी महासंघ (FIH)</b> द्वारा 21 वर्ष से कम आयु की पुरुष टीमों के लिए आयोजित होता है।<br>• भारत ने पुरुष जूनियर खिताब <b>दो बार</b>, <b>2001 तथा 2016</b> में जीता है, तथा <b>2021</b> में इसकी मेजबानी <b>भुवनेश्वर</b> में की थी।<br>• <b>तमिलनाडु</b> की हॉकी परंपरा मजबूत है, जहाँ <b>धनराज पिल्लै</b> जैसे खिलाड़ी हुए और चेन्नई का <b>मेयर राधाकृष्णन स्टेडियम</b> प्रमुख केंद्र है।<br>• भारत की सीनियर पुरुष टीम ने <b>टोक्यो 2020 ओलंपिक</b> तथा <b>पेरिस 2024 ओलंपिक</b> में <b>कांस्य</b> पदक जीता।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000070925","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"The shift from an officially administered exchange-rate system to a market-determined exchange-rate system is an example of which type of reform? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"आधिकारिक रूप से प्रशासित विनिमय दर प्रणाली से बाजार-निर्धारित विनिमय दर प्रणाली की ओर परिवर्तन किस प्रकार के सुधार का उदाहरण है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Industrial exchange policy reform","hi":"औद्योगिक विनिमय नीति सुधार"},"2":{"en":"Public-sector exchange ownership reform","hi":"सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र विनिमय स्वामित्व सुधार"},"3":{"en":"Fiscal exchange policy reform","hi":"राजकोषीय विनिमय नीति सुधार"},"4":{"en":"Foreign exchange reform","hi":"विदेशी मुद्रा सुधार"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Foreign exchange reform</b><br>The move from an <b>officially administered exchange rate</b> to a <b>market-determined exchange rate</b> is a <b>foreign exchange reform</b>, an important part of the 1991 reforms.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• In <b>July 1991</b>, the rupee was <b>devalued in two steps</b> by about 19%, and a <b>Liberalised Exchange Rate Management System (LERMS)</b> was introduced in 1992.<br>• In <b>1993</b>, India moved to a <b>unified market-determined exchange rate</b> with limited intervention by the Reserve Bank of India.<br>• The <b>Foreign Exchange Management Act (FEMA), 1999</b> replaced FERA and relaxed controls on foreign exchange transactions.<br>• The <b>current account</b> became fully convertible in <b>1994</b>, while the capital account remains partially convertible.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – विदेशी मुद्रा सुधार</b><br><b>आधिकारिक रूप से प्रशासित विनिमय दर</b> से <b>बाजार-निर्धारित विनिमय दर</b> की ओर परिवर्तन <b>विदेशी मुद्रा सुधार</b> है, जो 1991 के सुधारों का महत्वपूर्ण भाग था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>जुलाई 1991</b> में रुपये का <b>दो चरणों में अवमूल्यन</b> लगभग 19% किया गया तथा <b>1992</b> में <b>उदारीकृत विनिमय दर प्रबंधन प्रणाली (LERMS)</b> आरंभ हुई।<br>• <b>1993</b> में भारत ने भारतीय रिज़र्व बैंक के सीमित हस्तक्षेप के साथ <b>एकीकृत बाजार-निर्धारित विनिमय दर</b> अपनाई।<br>• <b>विदेशी मुद्रा प्रबंधन अधिनियम (FEMA), 1999</b> ने FERA का स्थान लिया और विदेशी मुद्रा लेनदेन पर नियंत्रण ढीले किए।<br>• <b>चालू खाता</b> <b>1994</b> में पूर्णतः परिवर्तनीय हुआ, जबकि पूंजी खाता आंशिक रूप से परिवर्तनीय है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000070926","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Reports and Indices","question":{"en":"Which of the following is a key principle underlying Ease of Doing Business (EoDB) reforms? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा व्यापार सुगमता (EoDB) सुधारों का प्रमुख सिद्धांत है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Promoting transparency and efficiency in regulatory processes","hi":"नियामक प्रक्रियाओं में पारदर्शिता तथा दक्षता को बढ़ावा देना"},"2":{"en":"Promoting secrecy and inefficiency in regulatory processes","hi":"नियामक प्रक्रियाओं में गोपनीयता तथा अक्षमता को बढ़ावा देना"},"3":{"en":"Promoting complexity and delays in regulatory processes","hi":"नियामक प्रक्रियाओं में जटिलता तथा विलंब को बढ़ावा देना"},"4":{"en":"Promoting multiple approvals and duplication in regulatory processes","hi":"नियामक प्रक्रियाओं में अनेक मंजूरियों तथा दोहराव को बढ़ावा देना"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Promoting transparency and efficiency in regulatory processes</b><br>A key principle of <b>Ease of Doing Business</b> reforms is <b>promoting transparency and efficiency</b> in regulatory processes by simplifying procedures and reducing compliance burden.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• EoDB reforms include <b>single-window clearances, online applications, time-bound approvals and decriminalisation of minor offences</b>.<br>• The <b>World Bank's Ease of Doing Business Index</b> measured economies on parameters such as starting a business, getting construction permits and enforcing contracts until the index was discontinued in <b>2021</b>.<br>• In India, the reforms are driven by the <b>Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal Trade (DPIIT)</b> through the <b>Business Reforms Action Plan</b>.<br>• Measures also include <b>reducing the number of licences, digital governance and the National Single Window System</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – नियामक प्रक्रियाओं में पारदर्शिता तथा दक्षता को बढ़ावा देना</b><br><b>व्यापार सुगमता</b> सुधारों का प्रमुख सिद्धांत प्रक्रियाओं को सरल करके तथा अनुपालन बोझ घटाकर <b>नियामक प्रक्रियाओं में पारदर्शिता तथा दक्षता</b> बढ़ाना है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• EoDB सुधारों में <b>एकल खिड़की मंजूरी, ऑनलाइन आवेदन, समयबद्ध स्वीकृति तथा लघु अपराधों का अपराधीकरण हटाना</b> शामिल है।<br>• <b>विश्व बैंक का व्यापार सुगमता सूचकांक</b> अर्थव्यवस्थाओं को व्यापार आरंभ, निर्माण अनुमति तथा अनुबंध प्रवर्तन जैसे मानकों पर मापता था; यह सूचकांक <b>2021</b> में बंद कर दिया गया।<br>• भारत में इन सुधारों का संचालन <b>उद्योग एवं आंतरिक व्यापार संवर्धन विभाग (DPIIT)</b> <b>व्यापार सुधार कार्य योजना</b> के माध्यम से करता है।<br>• उपायों में <b>लाइसेंसों की संख्या घटाना, डिजिटल शासन तथा राष्ट्रीय एकल खिड़की प्रणाली</b> भी शामिल हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000070927","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"As a result of post-1991 agricultural reforms, Indian policy encouraged a shift away from food grain production for domestic consumption. Under these new policy strategies, which of the following became the primary market for agricultural production? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"1991 के बाद के कृषि सुधारों के परिणामस्वरूप भारतीय नीति ने घरेलू उपभोग हेतु खाद्यान्न उत्पादन से दूर जाने को प्रोत्साहित किया। इन नई नीति रणनीतियों के अंतर्गत कृषि उत्पादन के लिए प्राथमिक बाजार कौन-सा बना? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Domestic consumer market","hi":"घरेलू उपभोक्ता बाजार"},"2":{"en":"International export market","hi":"अंतर्राष्ट्रीय निर्यात बाजार"},"3":{"en":"Regulated wholesale market","hi":"नियंत्रित थोक बाजार"},"4":{"en":"Cooperative procurement market","hi":"सहकारी खरीद बाजार"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – International export market</b><br>After the 1991 reforms, agricultural policy encouraged diversification towards <b>high-value crops</b> and the <b>international export market</b>, away from only food grains for domestic consumption.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Reforms included <b>liberalised trade, removal of quantitative restrictions, export incentives and a market-determined exchange rate</b>.<br>• Exports of <b>rice, wheat, spices, fruits, vegetables, marine products and buffalo meat</b> expanded after liberalisation.<br>• The shift also encouraged <b>horticulture, floriculture, dairy and processed food</b>, supported by schemes for <b>agri-export zones and food parks</b>.<br>• Critics note that this shift increased <b>regional imbalance and vulnerability to global price shocks</b> and reduced focus on coarse grains.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – अंतर्राष्ट्रीय निर्यात बाजार</b><br>1991 के सुधारों के बाद कृषि नीति ने केवल घरेलू उपभोग के खाद्यान्न से हटकर <b>उच्च मूल्य फसलों</b> तथा <b>अंतर्राष्ट्रीय निर्यात बाजार</b> की ओर विविधीकरण को प्रोत्साहित किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सुधारों में <b>उदारीकृत व्यापार, मात्रात्मक प्रतिबंधों की समाप्ति, निर्यात प्रोत्साहन तथा बाजार-निर्धारित विनिमय दर</b> शामिल थे।<br>• उदारीकरण के बाद <b>चावल, गेहूँ, मसाले, फल-सब्जियाँ, समुद्री उत्पाद तथा भैंस मांस</b> के निर्यात में विस्तार हुआ।<br>• इस बदलाव ने <b>बागवानी, पुष्पकृषि, डेयरी तथा प्रसंस्कृत खाद्य</b> को प्रोत्साहित किया, जिसे <b>कृषि निर्यात क्षेत्र तथा खाद्य पार्क</b> योजनाओं से सहारा मिला।<br>• आलोचकों के अनुसार इससे <b>क्षेत्रीय असंतुलन तथा वैश्विक मूल्य झटकों के प्रति संवेदनशीलता</b> बढ़ी और मोटे अनाजों पर ध्यान घटा।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000070928","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Ecosystem","question":{"en":"Which statement most accurately captures the relationship between biodiversity and human survival described? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कौन-सा कथन जैव विविधता तथा मानव अस्तित्व के वर्णित संबंध को सर्वाधिक सटीक रूप से प्रस्तुत करता है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Biodiversity has aesthetic value but no economic importance.","hi":"जैव विविधता का सौंदर्य मूल्य है परंतु आर्थिक महत्व नहीं है।"},"2":{"en":"Human societies function independently of ecosystems.","hi":"मानव समाज पारितंत्रों से स्वतंत्र रूप से कार्य करते हैं।"},"3":{"en":"Biodiversity provides essential ecosystem services.","hi":"जैव विविधता आवश्यक पारितंत्र सेवाएँ प्रदान करती है।"},"4":{"en":"Only domesticated species support human welfare.","hi":"केवल पालतू प्रजातियाँ मानव कल्याण का समर्थन करती हैं।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Biodiversity provides essential ecosystem services.</b><br><b>Biodiversity</b> supports human survival by providing <b>essential ecosystem services</b> such as food, clean water, pollination, climate regulation and nutrient cycling.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Ecosystem services are classified as <b>provisioning, regulating, supporting and cultural services</b> in the Millennium Ecosystem Assessment.<br>• <b>Pollinators, soil organisms and marine plankton</b> perform services worth trillions of dollars and cannot be replaced easily.<br>• Biodiversity also provides <b>medicines, genetic resources for crops and resilience against pests and climate change</b>.<br>• The <b>Convention on Biological Diversity (1992)</b> and the <b>Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework (2022)</b> guide global conservation efforts.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – जैव विविधता आवश्यक पारितंत्र सेवाएँ प्रदान करती है।</b><br><b>जैव विविधता</b> भोजन, स्वच्छ जल, परागण, जलवायु नियमन तथा पोषक पुनर्चक्रण जैसी <b>आवश्यक पारितंत्र सेवाएँ</b> प्रदान करके मानव अस्तित्व को सहारा देती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मिलेनियम पारितंत्र आकलन में पारितंत्र सेवाएँ <b>प्रदायक, नियामक, सहायक तथा सांस्कृतिक सेवाओं</b> में वर्गीकृत हैं।<br>• <b>परागणकर्ता, मृदा जीव तथा समुद्री प्लांकटन</b> खरबों डॉलर मूल्य की सेवाएँ देते हैं और इन्हें आसानी से बदला नहीं जा सकता।<br>• जैव विविधता <b>औषधियाँ, फसलों के आनुवंशिक संसाधन तथा कीट एवं जलवायु परिवर्तन के प्रति सहनशीलता</b> भी देती है।<br>• <b>जैव विविधता अभिसमय (1992)</b> तथा <b>कुनमिंग-मॉन्ट्रियल वैश्विक जैव विविधता ढाँचा (2022)</b> वैश्विक संरक्षण प्रयासों का मार्गदर्शन करते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000070929","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Basics of Environmental Sciences","question":{"en":"Large dams are often described as creating a \"development paradox\" because they: [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"बड़े बाँधों को प्रायः \"विकास विरोधाभास\" उत्पन्न करने वाला कहा जाता है क्योंकि वे: [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Completely fail to generate electricity and provide irrigation benefits.","hi":"विद्युत उत्पादन तथा सिंचाई लाभ देने में पूर्णतः असफल रहते हैं।"},"2":{"en":"Improve agricultural productivity and generate electricity without causing ecological damage.","hi":"पारिस्थितिक क्षति के बिना कृषि उत्पादकता सुधारते हैं तथा विद्युत उत्पन्न करते हैं।"},"3":{"en":"Promote economic growth while causing ecological and social disruption.","hi":"आर्थिक विकास को बढ़ावा देते हैं, जबकि पारिस्थितिक तथा सामाजिक विस्थापन उत्पन्न करते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Reduce irrigation efficiency and limit water availability in all regions.","hi":"सभी क्षेत्रों में सिंचाई दक्षता घटाते हैं तथा जल उपलब्धता सीमित करते हैं।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Promote economic growth while causing ecological and social disruption.</b><br>Large dams create a <b>development paradox</b> because they <b>promote economic growth</b> through irrigation, hydropower and flood control, but also cause <b>ecological damage and social displacement</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Benefits include <b>electricity, irrigation, drinking water and flood moderation</b>, which support agriculture and industry.<br>• Costs include <b>submergence of forests, loss of biodiversity, reservoir-induced seismicity, silting and displacement of communities</b>.<br>• The <b>World Commission on Dams (2000)</b> highlighted these trade-offs and recommended participatory decision-making.<br>• In India, movements such as the <b>Narmada Bachao Andolan</b> and the <b>Save Silent Valley</b> campaign raised these concerns.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – आर्थिक विकास को बढ़ावा देते हैं, जबकि पारिस्थितिक तथा सामाजिक विस्थापन उत्पन्न करते हैं।</b><br>बड़े बाँध <b>विकास विरोधाभास</b> उत्पन्न करते हैं क्योंकि वे सिंचाई, जलविद्युत तथा बाढ़ नियंत्रण से <b>आर्थिक विकास</b> को बढ़ावा देते हैं, परंतु साथ ही <b>पारिस्थितिक क्षति तथा सामाजिक विस्थापन</b> भी करते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• लाभों में <b>विद्युत, सिंचाई, पेयजल तथा बाढ़ नियंत्रण</b> शामिल हैं, जो कृषि तथा उद्योग को सहारा देते हैं।<br>• लागतों में <b>वनों का जलमग्न होना, जैव विविधता हानि, जलाशय प्रेरित भूकंपीयता, गाद तथा समुदायों का विस्थापन</b> शामिल है।<br>• <b>विश्व बाँध आयोग (2000)</b> ने इन अंतर्निहित विरोधाभासों को रेखांकित कर सहभागी निर्णय प्रक्रिया की सिफारिश की।<br>• भारत में <b>नर्मदा बचाओ आंदोलन</b> तथा <b>साइलेंट वैली बचाओ</b> अभियान ने इन चिंताओं को उठाया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000070930","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Basics of Economy","question":{"en":"Why is the demand for transportation regarded as a derived demand? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"परिवहन की माँग को व्युत्पन्न माँग क्यों माना जाता है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Transport demand arises from independent activities.","hi":"परिवहन माँग स्वतंत्र गतिविधियों से उत्पन्न होती है।"},"2":{"en":"Transport demand arises from other activities.","hi":"परिवहन माँग अन्य गतिविधियों से उत्पन्न होती है।"},"3":{"en":"Transport demand arises from luxury activities.","hi":"परिवहन माँग विलासिता गतिविधियों से उत्पन्न होती है।"},"4":{"en":"Transport demand arises from government policies.","hi":"परिवहन माँग सरकारी नीतियों से उत्पन्न होती है।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Transport demand arises from other activities.</b><br>The demand for transportation is a <b>derived demand</b> because it arises from the need to carry out <b>other activities</b>, such as going to work, transporting goods or accessing services.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Derived demand means demand for a good or service is not for its own sake but <b>for the utility it provides in another activity</b>.<br>• Transport demand is also influenced by <b>land use patterns, income levels, prices of fuel and availability of alternatives</b>.<br>• Similar derived demands are seen for <b>labour, raw materials and intermediate goods</b>, which depend on demand for final products.<br>• In economics, <b>direct demand</b> refers to demand for goods consumed for their own sake, such as food and clothing.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – परिवहन माँग अन्य गतिविधियों से उत्पन्न होती है।</b><br>परिवहन की माँग <b>व्युत्पन्न माँग</b> है क्योंकि यह <b>अन्य गतिविधियों</b> जैसे कार्यस्थल तक जाने, माल भेजने अथवा सेवाओं तक पहुँचने की आवश्यकता से उत्पन्न होती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• व्युत्पन्न माँग का अर्थ है कि किसी वस्तु अथवा सेवा की माँग स्वयं के लिए नहीं, बल्कि <b>अन्य गतिविधि में उसकी उपयोगिता</b> के लिए होती है।<br>• परिवहन माँग <b>भूमि उपयोग प्रारूप, आय स्तर, ईंधन मूल्य तथा विकल्पों की उपलब्धता</b> से भी प्रभावित होती है।<br>• इसी प्रकार <b>श्रम, कच्चे माल तथा मध्यवर्ती वस्तुओं</b> की माँग व्युत्पन्न होती है, जो अंतिम उत्पादों की माँग पर निर्भर करती है।<br>• अर्थशास्त्र में <b>प्रत्यक्ष माँग</b> उन वस्तुओं की माँग है जो स्वयं के उपभोग के लिए होती हैं, जैसे भोजन तथा वस्त्र।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000070931","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"Examine the frequency polygon showing student scores on a Math Test (out of 100). Answer the following question.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q51.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>What is the midpoint of the class interval with the highest frequency in this data set?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q51.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"गणित परीक्षा (100 में से) में विद्यार्थियों के अंकों को दर्शाने वाले बारंबारता बहुभुज का निरीक्षण कीजिए। निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q51.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>इस आँकड़े में सबसे अधिक बारंबारता वाले वर्ग अंतराल का मध्यबिंदु क्या है?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q51.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"52.5"},"2":{"en":"52"},"3":{"en":"45.2"},"4":{"en":"60.5"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The highest point of the polygon is at the class 45–60 with frequency 18<br>Midpoint = \\(\\frac{45 + 60}{2}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{52.5}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 52.5.</b>","hi":"बहुभुज का उच्चतम बिंदु वर्ग 45–60 पर है, जिसकी बारंबारता 18 है<br>मध्यबिंदु = \\(\\frac{45 + 60}{2}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{52.5}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 52.5 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q51.jpg"]}},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000070932","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"Which of the following is the correct fractional representation of the recurring decimal \\(0.12\\overline{3}\\)? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा आवर्ती दशमलव \\(0.12\\overline{3}\\) का सही भिन्नात्मक निरूपण है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{111}{990}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{123}{999}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{41}{333}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{37}{300}\\)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(0.12\\overline{3} = \\frac{123 - 12}{900}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{111}{900}\\)<br>Dividing by 3: \\(\\frac{37}{300}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{37}{300}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(\\frac{37}{300}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(0.12\\overline{3} = \\frac{123 - 12}{900}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{111}{900}\\)<br>3 से भाग देने पर: \\(\\frac{37}{300}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{37}{300}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(\\frac{37}{300}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000070933","section":"MATH","topic":"Time Speed and Distance","question":{"en":"A bus runs at 40 km/h and reaches its destination 18 minutes late. When its speed is increased to 50 km/h, it reaches 6 minutes early. Find the distance covered by the bus. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक बस 40 km/h की चाल से चलती है और अपने गंतव्य पर 18 मिनट देर से पहुँचती है। जब उसकी चाल 50 km/h कर दी जाती है, तो वह 6 मिनट पहले पहुँच जाती है। बस द्वारा तय की गई दूरी ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"60 km"},"2":{"en":"80 km"},"3":{"en":"100 km"},"4":{"en":"120 km"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Difference of times = \\(18 + 6 = 24\\) minutes = \\(\\frac{2}{5}\\) h<br>\\(\\frac{d}{40} - \\frac{d}{50} = \\frac{2}{5}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{d}{200} = \\frac{2}{5}\\)<br>\\(d = \\boxed{80}\\) km<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 80 km.</b>","hi":"समयों का अंतर = \\(18 + 6 = 24\\) मिनट = \\(\\frac{2}{5}\\) घंटे<br>\\(\\frac{d}{40} - \\frac{d}{50} = \\frac{2}{5}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{d}{200} = \\frac{2}{5}\\)<br>\\(d = \\boxed{80}\\) km<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 80 km है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000070934","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Find the value of \\(\\frac{(2.3)^3 - (0.3)^3}{(2.3)^2 + 0.69 + (0.3)^2}\\). [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"\\(\\frac{(2.3)^3 - (0.3)^3}{(2.3)^2 + 0.69 + (0.3)^2}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"6"},"4":{"en":"8"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Here \\(a = 2.3\\), \\(b = 0.3\\) and \\(ab = 2.3 \\times 0.3 = 0.69\\)<br>\\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2} = a - b\\)<br>\\(= 2.3 - 0.3 = \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 2.</b>","hi":"यहाँ \\(a = 2.3\\), \\(b = 0.3\\) और \\(ab = 2.3 \\times 0.3 = 0.69\\)<br>\\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2} = a - b\\)<br>\\(= 2.3 - 0.3 = \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000070935","section":"MATH","topic":"LCM and HCF","question":{"en":"How many numbers are there from 100 to 300 which are divisible by both 4 and 6? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"100 से 300 तक ऐसी कितनी संख्याएँ हैं जो 4 और 6 दोनों से विभाज्य हैं? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"16"},"2":{"en":"17"},"3":{"en":"18"},"4":{"en":"20"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Numbers divisible by both 4 and 6 are multiples of LCM(4, 6) = 12<br>First multiple ≥ 100 is 108, last ≤ 300 is 300<br>Count = \\(\\frac{300}{12} - \\frac{108}{12} + 1 = 25 - 9 + 1\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{17}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 17.</b>","hi":"4 और 6 दोनों से विभाज्य संख्याएँ LCM(4, 6) = 12 के गुणज हैं<br>100 से बड़ा पहला गुणज 108 है, 300 तक अंतिम 300 है<br>संख्या = \\(\\frac{300}{12} - \\frac{108}{12} + 1 = 25 - 9 + 1\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{17}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 17 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000070936","section":"MATH","topic":"Partnership","question":{"en":"A, B, and C are partners in a business. A invested a certain amount for 6 months and claims \\(\\frac{1}{8}\\) of the profit. B invested a certain amount for 9 months and claims \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) of the profit. C invested ₹1,560 for 12 months. Find the amount invested by A. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"A, B और C एक व्यवसाय में साझेदार हैं। A ने 6 महीने के लिए एक निश्चित राशि निवेश की और लाभ का \\(\\frac{1}{8}\\) भाग दावा करता है। B ने 9 महीने के लिए एक निश्चित राशि निवेश की और लाभ का \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) भाग दावा करता है। C ने 12 महीनों के लिए ₹1,560 निवेश किए। A द्वारा निवेश की गई राशि ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹800"},"2":{"en":"₹780"},"3":{"en":"₹720"},"4":{"en":"₹640"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Shares: A = \\(\\frac{1}{8}\\), B = \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\), so C = \\(1 - \\left(\\frac{1}{8} + \\frac{1}{3}\\right) = \\frac{13}{24}\\)<br>C's capital-months = \\(1560 \\times 12 = 18720\\)<br>A's capital-months = \\(\\frac{3}{13} \\times 18720 = 4320\\)<br>A's investment = \\(\\frac{4320}{6} = \\boxed{720}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): ₹720.</b>","hi":"हिस्से: A = \\(\\frac{1}{8}\\), B = \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\), अतः C = \\(1 - \\left(\\frac{1}{8} + \\frac{1}{3}\\right) = \\frac{13}{24}\\)<br>C की पूँजी-महीने = \\(1560 \\times 12 = 18720\\)<br>A की पूँजी-महीने = \\(\\frac{3}{13} \\times 18720 = 4320\\)<br>A का निवेश = \\(\\frac{4320}{6} = \\boxed{720}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): ₹720 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000070937","section":"MATH","topic":"Average","question":{"en":"If the average temperature for Monday, Tuesday, and Wednesday was 40°C. The average for Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday was 40°C. If the temperature on Thursday was 40°C, what was the temperature on Monday? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि सोमवार, मंगलवार और बुधवार का औसत तापमान 40°C था। मंगलवार, बुधवार और गुरुवार का औसत 40°C था। यदि गुरुवार का तापमान 40°C था, तो सोमवार का तापमान क्या था? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"50°C"},"2":{"en":"40°C"},"3":{"en":"30°C"},"4":{"en":"20°C"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Mon + Tue + Wed = \\(40 \\times 3 = 120\\)<br>Tue + Wed + Thu = \\(40 \\times 3 = 120\\), with Thu = 40<br>So Tue + Wed = 80<br>Mon = \\(120 - 80 = \\boxed{40}\\)°C<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 40°C.</b>","hi":"सोम + मंगल + बुध = \\(40 \\times 3 = 120\\)<br>मंगल + बुध + गुरु = \\(40 \\times 3 = 120\\), गुरु = 40<br>अतः मंगल + बुध = 80<br>सोम = \\(120 - 80 = \\boxed{40}\\)°C<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 40°C है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000070938","section":"MATH","topic":"Coordinate Geometry","question":{"en":"A line L has a slope of -1 and passes through the point (4, 4). What is the area of the triangle formed by this line and the coordinate axes? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"रेखा L का ढाल -1 है और यह बिंदु (4, 4) से गुजरती है। इस रेखा और निर्देशांक अक्षों से बने त्रिभुज का क्षेत्रफल क्या है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"24 square units","hi":"24 वर्ग इकाई"},"2":{"en":"32 square units","hi":"32 वर्ग इकाई"},"3":{"en":"16 square units","hi":"16 वर्ग इकाई"},"4":{"en":"64 square units","hi":"64 वर्ग इकाई"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"220\" height=\"200\" viewBox=\"0 0 220 200\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M30 165H200\"/><path d=\"M45 45V180\"/><path d=\"M45 67L141 165\"/><path d=\"M93 116V165M93 116H45\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><circle cx=\"93\" cy=\"116\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"99\" y=\"111\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">(4, 4)</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"111\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">(4, 4)</text><text x=\"38\" y=\"71\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">8</text><text x=\"38\" y=\"71\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">8</text><text x=\"145\" y=\"192\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">8</text><text x=\"145\" y=\"192\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">8</text><text x=\"204\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">x</text><text x=\"204\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">x</text><text x=\"51\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">y</text><text x=\"51\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">y</text></g></svg><br>Line: \\(y - 4 = -1(x - 4) \\Rightarrow y = -x + 8\\)<br>Intercepts on both axes = 8<br>Area = \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times 8 \\times 8 = \\boxed{32}\\) square units<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 32 square units.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"220\" height=\"200\" viewBox=\"0 0 220 200\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M30 165H200\"/><path d=\"M45 45V180\"/><path d=\"M45 67L141 165\"/><path d=\"M93 116V165M93 116H45\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><circle cx=\"93\" cy=\"116\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"99\" y=\"111\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">(4, 4)</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"111\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">(4, 4)</text><text x=\"38\" y=\"71\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">8</text><text x=\"38\" y=\"71\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">8</text><text x=\"145\" y=\"192\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">8</text><text x=\"145\" y=\"192\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">8</text><text x=\"204\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">x</text><text x=\"204\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">x</text><text x=\"51\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">y</text><text x=\"51\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">y</text></g></svg><br>रेखा: \\(y - 4 = -1(x - 4) \\Rightarrow y = -x + 8\\)<br>दोनों अक्षों पर अंतःखंड = 8<br>क्षेत्रफल = \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times 8 \\times 8 = \\boxed{32}\\) वर्ग इकाई<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 32 वर्ग इकाई है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000070939","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A cube with diagonal \\(30\\sqrt{3}\\) cm is melted to make a cuboid. The length of the cuboid is equal to the side of the cube and the breadth is 15 cm. Find the height. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"\\(30\\sqrt{3}\\) cm विकर्ण वाले एक घन को पिघलाकर एक घनाभ बनाया जाता है। घनाभ की लंबाई घन की भुजा के बराबर है और चौड़ाई 15 cm है। ऊँचाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"38 cm"},"2":{"en":"60 cm"},"3":{"en":"45 cm"},"4":{"en":"52 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"310\" height=\"190\" viewBox=\"0 0 310 190\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M40 40H130V130H40Z\"/><path d=\"M80 14H170V104H80Z\"/><path d=\"M40 40L80 14M130 40L170 14M130 130L170 104\"/><path d=\"M40 130L170 14\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M182 76H204M198 70L204 76L198 82\"/><path d=\"M218 35H248V155H218Z\"/><path d=\"M240 22H270V142H240Z\"/><path d=\"M218 35L240 22M248 35L270 22M248 155L270 142\"/><text x=\"85\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">30</text><text x=\"85\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">30</text><text x=\"98\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">30√3</text><text x=\"98\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">30√3</text><text x=\"231\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">15</text><text x=\"231\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">15</text><text x=\"212\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">h</text><text x=\"212\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">h</text><text x=\"276\" y=\"142\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">30</text><text x=\"276\" y=\"142\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">30</text></g></svg><br>\\(a\\sqrt{3} = 30\\sqrt{3} \\Rightarrow a = 30\\) cm<br>Volume of the cube = \\(30^3 = 27000\\) cm³<br>\\(30 \\times 15 \\times h = 27000\\)<br>\\(h = \\frac{27000}{450} = \\boxed{60}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 60 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"310\" height=\"190\" viewBox=\"0 0 310 190\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M40 40H130V130H40Z\"/><path d=\"M80 14H170V104H80Z\"/><path d=\"M40 40L80 14M130 40L170 14M130 130L170 104\"/><path d=\"M40 130L170 14\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M182 76H204M198 70L204 76L198 82\"/><path d=\"M218 35H248V155H218Z\"/><path d=\"M240 22H270V142H240Z\"/><path d=\"M218 35L240 22M248 35L270 22M248 155L270 142\"/><text x=\"85\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">30</text><text x=\"85\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">30</text><text x=\"98\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">30√3</text><text x=\"98\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">30√3</text><text x=\"231\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">15</text><text x=\"231\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">15</text><text x=\"212\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">h</text><text x=\"212\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">h</text><text x=\"276\" y=\"142\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">30</text><text x=\"276\" y=\"142\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">30</text></g></svg><br>\\(a\\sqrt{3} = 30\\sqrt{3} \\Rightarrow a = 30\\) cm<br>घन का आयतन = \\(30^3 = 27000\\) cm³<br>\\(30 \\times 15 \\times h = 27000\\)<br>\\(h = \\frac{27000}{450} = \\boxed{60}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 60 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000070940","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"A machine rotates at 30π radians per second. Find the number of revolutions it makes in one minute. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक मशीन 30π रेडियन प्रति सेकंड घूमती है। एक मिनट में वह कितने चक्कर लगाएगी? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"400"},"2":{"en":"600"},"3":{"en":"500"},"4":{"en":"900"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Angle turned in 1 minute = \\(30\\pi \\times 60 = 1800\\pi\\) radians<br>One revolution = \\(2\\pi\\) radians<br>Revolutions = \\(\\frac{1800\\pi}{2\\pi} = \\boxed{900}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 900.</b>","hi":"1 मिनट में घूमा कोण = \\(30\\pi \\times 60 = 1800\\pi\\) रेडियन<br>एक चक्कर = \\(2\\pi\\) रेडियन<br>चक्कर = \\(\\frac{1800\\pi}{2\\pi} = \\boxed{900}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 900 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000070941","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If sinθ = \\(\\frac{8}{17}\\) and θ is an acute angle, find the value of 6(cosecθ – cotθ). [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि sinθ = \\(\\frac{8}{17}\\) और θ न्यून कोण है, तो 6(cosecθ – cotθ) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{3}{2}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{4}{3}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{5}{2}\\)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\cos\\theta = \\sqrt{1 - \\frac{64}{289}} = \\frac{15}{17}\\)<br>\\(\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta = \\frac{17}{8}\\), \\(\\cot\\theta = \\frac{15}{8}\\)<br>\\(6\\left(\\frac{17}{8} - \\frac{15}{8}\\right) = 6 \\times \\frac{2}{8}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{3}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(\\frac{3}{2}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\cos\\theta = \\sqrt{1 - \\frac{64}{289}} = \\frac{15}{17}\\)<br>\\(\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta = \\frac{17}{8}\\), \\(\\cot\\theta = \\frac{15}{8}\\)<br>\\(6\\left(\\frac{17}{8} - \\frac{15}{8}\\right) = 6 \\times \\frac{2}{8}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{3}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(\\frac{3}{2}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000070942","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{10+y} + \\sqrt{10-y}}{\\sqrt{10+y} - \\sqrt{10-y}} = 4\\),then find the value of y. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{10+y} + \\sqrt{10-y}}{\\sqrt{10+y} - \\sqrt{10-y}} = 4\\) है, तो y का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{80}{17}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{40}{19}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{3}{4}\\)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let \\(\\sqrt{10+y} = u\\) and \\(\\sqrt{10-y} = v\\).<br>\\(\\frac{u+v}{u-v} = 4 \\Rightarrow u+v = 4u-4v \\Rightarrow 5v = 3u \\Rightarrow \\frac{u}{v} = \\frac{5}{3}\\)<br>Squaring: \\(\\frac{10+y}{10-y} = \\frac{25}{9}\\)<br>\\(90 + 9y = 250 - 25y \\Rightarrow 34y = 160\\)<br>\\(y = \\boxed{\\frac{80}{17}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(\\frac{80}{17}\\).</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए \\(\\sqrt{10+y} = u\\) और \\(\\sqrt{10-y} = v\\)<br>\\(\\frac{u+v}{u-v} = 4 \\Rightarrow u+v = 4u-4v \\Rightarrow 5v = 3u \\Rightarrow \\frac{u}{v} = \\frac{5}{3}\\)<br>वर्ग करने पर: \\(\\frac{10+y}{10-y} = \\frac{25}{9}\\)<br>\\(90 + 9y = 250 - 25y \\Rightarrow 34y = 160\\)<br>\\(y = \\boxed{\\frac{80}{17}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(\\frac{80}{17}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000070943","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"Tea costing ₹126 per kg and ₹135 per kg are mixed with a third variety in the ratio 1: 1: 2. If the resulting mixture is valued at ₹153 per kg, find the price per kg of the third variety. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"₹126 प्रति kg और ₹135 प्रति kg वाली चाय को एक तीसरी किस्म के साथ 1: 1: 2 के अनुपात में मिलाया जाता है। यदि परिणामी मिश्रण का मूल्य ₹153 प्रति kg है, तो तीसरी किस्म का प्रति kg मूल्य ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹167.50 per kg","hi":"₹167.50 प्रति kg"},"2":{"en":"₹170 per kg","hi":"₹170 प्रति kg"},"3":{"en":"₹175.50 per kg","hi":"₹175.50 प्रति kg"},"4":{"en":"₹180 per kg","hi":"₹180 प्रति kg"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Let the third variety cost ₹x per kg; take 1, 1, 2 kg.<br>\\(\\frac{126 + 135 + 2x}{1 + 1 + 2} = 153\\)<br>\\(261 + 2x = 612 \\Rightarrow 2x = 351\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{175.50}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): ₹175.50 per kg.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए तीसरी किस्म ₹x प्रति kg है; 1, 1, 2 kg लीजिए।<br>\\(\\frac{126 + 135 + 2x}{1 + 1 + 2} = 153\\)<br>\\(261 + 2x = 612 \\Rightarrow 2x = 351\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{175.50}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): ₹175.50 प्रति kg है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000070944","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"The pie chart shows the percentage distribution of corporate staff members across different functional departments in an organization. Study the following pie chart carefully and answer the question that follows.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q64.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>If the total number of employees in the HR department is 120, what is the difference between the combined number of employees in the Engineering and Sales departments and the combined number of employees in the Marketing and Operations departments?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q64.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"पाई चार्ट किसी संगठन में विभिन्न कार्यात्मक विभागों में कॉर्पोरेट कर्मचारियों के प्रतिशत-वार वितरण को दर्शाता है। निम्नलिखित पाई चार्ट का ध्यानपूर्वक अध्ययन कीजिए और आगे दिए गए प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q64.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>यदि HR विभाग में कर्मचारियों की कुल संख्या 120 है, तो इंजीनियरिंग और सेल्स विभागों में कर्मचारियों की संयुक्त संख्या तथा मार्केटिंग और ऑपरेशंस विभागों में कर्मचारियों की संयुक्त संख्या के बीच का अंतर क्या है?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q64.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"240"},"2":{"en":"360"},"3":{"en":"480"},"4":{"en":"560"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"HR = 10% = 120 \\(\\Rightarrow\\) total employees = 1200<br>Engineering + Sales = \\(35\\% + 25\\% = 60\\%\\) = 720<br>Marketing + Operations = \\(15\\% + 15\\% = 30\\%\\) = 360<br>Difference = \\(720 - 360 = \\boxed{360}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 360.</b>","hi":"HR = 10% = 120 \\(\\Rightarrow\\) कुल कर्मचारी = 1200<br>इंजीनियरिंग + सेल्स = \\(35\\% + 25\\% = 60\\%\\) = 720<br>मार्केटिंग + ऑपरेशंस = \\(15\\% + 15\\% = 30\\%\\) = 360<br>अंतर = \\(720 - 360 = \\boxed{360}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 360 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q64.jpg"]}},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000070945","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If \\(\\sin\\theta + \\cos\\theta = \\sqrt{2}\\cos\\theta\\) for an acute angle θ, then what is the value of \\(\\cos\\theta - \\sin\\theta\\)? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि न्यून कोण θ के लिए \\(\\sin\\theta + \\cos\\theta = \\sqrt{2}\\cos\\theta\\) है, तो \\(\\cos\\theta - \\sin\\theta\\) का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{2}\\sin\\theta\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{2}\\cos\\theta\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\sin\\theta\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{3}\\cos\\theta\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sin\\theta + \\cos\\theta = \\sqrt{2}\\cos\\theta \\Rightarrow \\sin\\theta = (\\sqrt{2} - 1)\\cos\\theta\\)<br>So \\(\\tan\\theta = \\sqrt{2} - 1\\), which gives \\(\\theta = 22.5^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\cos\\theta - \\sin\\theta = \\cos\\theta - (\\sqrt{2} - 1)\\cos\\theta = (2 - \\sqrt{2})\\cos\\theta\\)<br>And \\(\\sqrt{2}\\sin\\theta = \\sqrt{2}(\\sqrt{2} - 1)\\cos\\theta = (2 - \\sqrt{2})\\cos\\theta\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\sqrt{2}\\sin\\theta}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(\\sqrt{2}\\sin\\theta\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\sin\\theta + \\cos\\theta = \\sqrt{2}\\cos\\theta \\Rightarrow \\sin\\theta = (\\sqrt{2} - 1)\\cos\\theta\\)<br>अतः \\(\\tan\\theta = \\sqrt{2} - 1\\), जिससे \\(\\theta = 22.5^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\cos\\theta - \\sin\\theta = \\cos\\theta - (\\sqrt{2} - 1)\\cos\\theta = (2 - \\sqrt{2})\\cos\\theta\\)<br>और \\((2 - \\sqrt{2})\\cos\\theta = \\sqrt{2}\\sin\\theta\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\sqrt{2}\\sin\\theta}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(\\sqrt{2}\\sin\\theta\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000070946","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"Machine X can purify a batch of chemicals in 12 hours. Machine Y can purify the same batch in 16 hours. A lab technician turns on Machine X and leaves the room. She returns after 5 hours and turns on Machine Y also to assist. From that point, how many hours will it take to complete purifying the rest of the batch? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"मशीन X रसायनों के एक बैच को 12 घंटे में शुद्ध कर सकती है। मशीन Y वही बैच 16 घंटे में शुद्ध कर सकती है। एक प्रयोगशाला तकनीशियन मशीन X चालू करके कक्ष से बाहर चली जाती है। 5 घंटे बाद लौटकर वह सहायता के लिए मशीन Y भी चालू कर देती है। उसके बाद शेष बैच को शुद्ध करने में कितने घंटे लगेंगे? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4 hrs"},"2":{"en":"6 hrs"},"3":{"en":"8 hrs"},"4":{"en":"9 hrs"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Work = 48 units \\(\\Rightarrow\\) X = 4 units/h, Y = 3 units/h<br>Work done by X in 5 hours = \\(4 \\times 5 = 20\\)<br>Remaining = \\(48 - 20 = 28\\) units<br>Together = \\(4 + 3 = 7\\) units/h<br>Time = \\(\\frac{28}{7} = \\boxed{4}\\) hrs<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 4 hrs.</b>","hi":"कार्य = 48 इकाई \\(\\Rightarrow\\) X = 4 इकाई/घंटा, Y = 3 इकाई/घंटा<br>X ने 5 घंटे में किया = \\(4 \\times 5 = 20\\)<br>शेष = \\(48 - 20 = 28\\) इकाई<br>दोनों मिलकर = \\(4 + 3 = 7\\) इकाई/घंटा<br>समय = \\(\\frac{28}{7} = \\boxed{4}\\) घंटे<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 4 hrs है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000070947","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If x = A sinθ and y = A cosθ, find x² + y². [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि x = A sinθ और y = A cosθ है, तो x² + y² ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A"},"2":{"en":"A²"},"3":{"en":"2A²"},"4":{"en":"0"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(x^2 + y^2 = A^2\\sin^2\\theta + A^2\\cos^2\\theta\\)<br>\\(= A^2(\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta)\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{A^2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): A².</b>","hi":"\\(x^2 + y^2 = A^2\\sin^2\\theta + A^2\\cos^2\\theta\\)<br>\\(= A^2(\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta)\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{A^2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): A² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000070948","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If a + b = 12, ab = 20, find a⁴ + b⁴. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि a + b = 12, ab = 20 है, तो a⁴ + b⁴ ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"10000"},"2":{"en":"10816"},"3":{"en":"10016"},"4":{"en":"11616"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(a^2 + b^2 = (a + b)^2 - 2ab = 144 - 40 = 104\\)<br>\\(a^4 + b^4 = (a^2 + b^2)^2 - 2a^2b^2\\)<br>\\(= 104^2 - 2(400) = 10816 - 800\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{10016}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 10016.</b>","hi":"\\(a^2 + b^2 = (a + b)^2 - 2ab = 144 - 40 = 104\\)<br>\\(a^4 + b^4 = (a^2 + b^2)^2 - 2a^2b^2\\)<br>\\(= 104^2 - 2(400) = 10816 - 800\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{10016}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 10016 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000070949","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In ΔABC, the angle bisector of ∠A is also a median of the triangle. Which of the following statements must always be true? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"ΔABC में, ∠A का कोण समद्विभाजक त्रिभुज की माध्यिका भी है। निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कथन सदैव सत्य होगा? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"AB = AC"},"2":{"en":"∠A = 90°"},"3":{"en":"BC = 2AB"},"4":{"en":"AB = 2AC"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"240\" height=\"190\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 190\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M120 38L50 162H190Z\"/><path d=\"M120 38V162\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M84 155V169M156 155V169\"/><path d=\"M120 58A20 20 0 0 0 103 52\"/><path d=\"M120 58A20 20 0 0 1 137 52\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"162\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"32\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"32\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B</text><text x=\"198\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">C</text><text x=\"198\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">C</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">D</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">D</text></g></svg><br>Angle bisector theorem: \\(\\frac{AB}{AC} = \\frac{BD}{DC}\\)<br>Since AD is also a median, \\(BD = DC\\), so \\(\\frac{AB}{AC} = 1\\)<br>\\(\\boxed{AB = AC}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): AB = AC.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"240\" height=\"190\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 190\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M120 38L50 162H190Z\"/><path d=\"M120 38V162\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M84 155V169M156 155V169\"/><path d=\"M120 58A20 20 0 0 0 103 52\"/><path d=\"M120 58A20 20 0 0 1 137 52\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"162\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"32\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"32\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B</text><text x=\"198\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">C</text><text x=\"198\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">C</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">D</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">D</text></g></svg><br>कोण समद्विभाजक प्रमेय: \\(\\frac{AB}{AC} = \\frac{BD}{DC}\\)<br>चूँकि AD माध्यिका भी है, \\(BD = DC\\), अतः \\(\\frac{AB}{AC} = 1\\)<br>\\(\\boxed{AB = AC}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): AB = AC है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000070950","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Simplify the following expression completely:<br>\\((\\sqrt{7} + \\sqrt{3})^2 - (\\sqrt{7} - \\sqrt{3})^2\\) [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित व्यंजक को पूर्णतः सरल कीजिए:<br>\\((\\sqrt{7} + \\sqrt{3})^2 - (\\sqrt{7} - \\sqrt{3})^2\\) [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0"},"2":{"en":"\\(2\\sqrt{21}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(6\\sqrt{21}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(4\\sqrt{21}\\)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\((a + b)^2 - (a - b)^2 = 4ab\\)<br>Here \\(a = \\sqrt{7}\\), \\(b = \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(= 4\\sqrt{7}\\sqrt{3} = \\boxed{4\\sqrt{21}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(4\\sqrt{21}\\).</b>","hi":"\\((a + b)^2 - (a - b)^2 = 4ab\\)<br>यहाँ \\(a = \\sqrt{7}\\), \\(b = \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(= 4\\sqrt{7}\\sqrt{3} = \\boxed{4\\sqrt{21}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(4\\sqrt{21}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000070951","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two concentric coplanar circles have radii 4 cm and 9 cm. How many common tangents can be drawn to these circles? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दो संकेंद्री समतलीय वृत्तों की त्रिज्याएँ 4 cm और 9 cm हैं। इन वृत्तों पर कितनी उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखाएँ खींची जा सकती हैं? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"2"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"260\" height=\"215\" viewBox=\"0 0 260 215\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"105\" r=\"40\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"105\" r=\"92\"/><path d=\"M120 105H160M120 105V13\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"105\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"142\" y=\"99\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">4</text><text x=\"142\" y=\"99\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">4</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">O</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">O</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"62\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">9</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"62\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">9</text></g></svg><br>Concentric circles have the same centre, so no line can touch both<br>Number of common tangents = \\(\\boxed{0}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 0.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"260\" height=\"215\" viewBox=\"0 0 260 215\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"105\" r=\"40\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"105\" r=\"92\"/><path d=\"M120 105H160M120 105V13\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"105\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"142\" y=\"99\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">4</text><text x=\"142\" y=\"99\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">4</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">O</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">O</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"62\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">9</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"62\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">9</text></g></svg><br>संकेंद्री वृत्तों का केंद्र एक ही होता है, अतः कोई रेखा दोनों को स्पर्श नहीं कर सकती<br>उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखाओं की संख्या = \\(\\boxed{0}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 0 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000070952","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"A psychological research study analyzes the frequency distribution of spatial-coordination errors made by participants using a complex flight simulator layout. The observations are illustrated in the bar graph below:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q72.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>Find the absolute difference between the median value and the arithmetic (weighted) mean of the given distribution.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q72.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक मनोवैज्ञानिक शोध अध्ययन जटिल फ्लाइट सिमुलेटर लेआउट का उपयोग करते हुए प्रतिभागियों द्वारा की गई स्थानिक-समन्वय त्रुटियों के बारंबारता वितरण का विश्लेषण करता है। प्रेक्षण नीचे दिए गए बार ग्राफ में दर्शाए गए हैं:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q72.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>दिए गए वितरण के माध्यक मान और समांतर (भारित) माध्य के बीच निरपेक्ष अंतर ज्ञात कीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q72.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0.36"},"2":{"en":"0.43"},"3":{"en":"0.55"},"4":{"en":"0.60"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Errors (x)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">0</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">f</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">30</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">17</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">22</td></tr></table><br>Mean = \\(\\frac{0(8) + 1(15) + 2(22) + 3(30) + 4(17) + 5(8)}{100} = \\frac{243}{100} = 2.43\\)<br>Total frequency = 100, so the median is the average of the 50th and 51st values<br>Cumulative: 8, 23, 45, 75 \\(\\Rightarrow\\) both lie in \\(x = 3\\), median = 2<br>Absolute difference = \\(\\boxed{0.43}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 0.43.</b>","hi":"<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">त्रुटियाँ (x)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">0</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">f</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">30</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">17</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">22</td></tr></table><br>माध्य = \\(\\frac{0(8) + 1(15) + 2(22) + 3(30) + 4(17) + 5(8)}{100} = \\frac{243}{100} = 2.43\\)<br>कुल बारंबारता = 100, अतः माध्यक 50वें और 51वें मान का औसत है<br>संचयी: 8, 23, 45, 75 \\(\\Rightarrow\\) दोनों \\(x = 3\\) में हैं, माध्यक = 2<br>निरपेक्ष अंतर = \\(\\boxed{0.43}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 0.43 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q72.jpg"]}},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000070953","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"Anurag and Bhavya have equal savings. Anurag invests all his savings at 10% compound interest per annum for 2 years. Bhavya invests \\(66\\frac{2}{3}\\)% of her savings at R% simple interest per annum and the remaining \\(33\\frac{1}{3}\\)% at 6% simple interest per annum, both for 2 years. If their interests are equal, what is R + \\(7\\frac{1}{4}\\)? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"अनुराग और भव्या की बचत बराबर है। अनुराग अपनी पूरी बचत 10% वार्षिक चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज पर 2 वर्षों के लिए निवेश करता है। भव्या अपनी बचत का \\(66\\frac{2}{3}\\)% भाग R% वार्षिक साधारण ब्याज पर और शेष \\(33\\frac{1}{3}\\)% भाग 6% वार्षिक साधारण ब्याज पर, दोनों 2 वर्षों के लिए निवेश करती है। यदि उनके ब्याज बराबर हैं, तो R + \\(7\\frac{1}{4}\\) क्या है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20%"},"2":{"en":"18%"},"3":{"en":"21%"},"4":{"en":"22%"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Let the savings be ₹100 each.<br>Anurag's interest = \\(100\\left(1.1^2 - 1\\right) = 21\\)<br>Bhavya: \\(\\frac{66\\frac{2}{3} \\times R \\times 2}{100} + \\frac{33\\frac{1}{3} \\times 6 \\times 2}{100} = 21\\)<br>\\(\\frac{400R}{300} + 4 = 21 \\Rightarrow \\frac{4R}{3} = 17 \\Rightarrow R = 12.75\\)<br>\\(R + 7\\frac{1}{4} = 12.75 + 7.25 = \\boxed{20}\\)%<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 20%.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए प्रत्येक की बचत ₹100 है।<br>अनुराग का ब्याज = \\(100\\left(1.1^2 - 1\\right) = 21\\)<br>भव्या: \\(\\frac{66\\frac{2}{3} \\times R \\times 2}{100} + \\frac{33\\frac{1}{3} \\times 6 \\times 2}{100} = 21\\)<br>\\(\\frac{400R}{300} + 4 = 21 \\Rightarrow \\frac{4R}{3} = 17 \\Rightarrow R = 12.75\\)<br>\\(R + 7\\frac{1}{4} = 12.75 + 7.25 = \\boxed{20}\\)%<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 20% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000070954","section":"MATH","topic":"Ratio and Proportion","question":{"en":"A prize fund is divided among P, Q and R directly in proportion to the squares of their scores and inversely in proportion to their ages. Their scores are in the ratio 2 : 3 : 4 and their ages in the ratio 3 : 4 : 5. If R receives ₹33,600 more than P, how much does Q receive? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक पुरस्कार निधि को P, Q और R के बीच उनके अंकों के वर्गों के सीधे अनुपात में और उनकी आयु के व्युत्क्रम अनुपात में बाँटा जाता है। उनके अंक 2 : 3 : 4 के अनुपात में और आयु 3 : 4 : 5 के अनुपात में हैं। यदि R को P से ₹33,600 अधिक मिलते हैं, तो Q को कितने मिलते हैं? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹ 38,400"},"2":{"en":"₹39,600"},"3":{"en":"₹40,000"},"4":{"en":"₹40,500"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Share ∝ \\(\\frac{\\text{score}^2}{\\text{age}}\\)<br>P : Q : R = \\(\\frac{4}{3} : \\frac{9}{4} : \\frac{16}{5} = 80 : 135 : 192\\)<br>\\(R - P = 192 - 80 = 112\\) parts = ₹33,600<br>1 part = ₹300<br>Q's share = \\(135 \\times 300 = \\boxed{40500}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): ₹40,500.</b>","hi":"हिस्सा ∝ \\(\\frac{\\text{अंक}^2}{\\text{आयु}}\\)<br>P : Q : R = \\(\\frac{4}{3} : \\frac{9}{4} : \\frac{16}{5} = 80 : 135 : 192\\)<br>\\(R - P = 192 - 80 = 112\\) भाग = ₹33,600<br>1 भाग = ₹300<br>Q का हिस्सा = \\(135 \\times 300 = \\boxed{40500}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): ₹40,500 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000070955","section":"MATH","topic":"Simple Interest (SI)","question":{"en":"A loan of ₹18,000 is repaid in 11 equal monthly instalments of ₹1,800 each, payable at the end of successive months starting from the first month. If interest is simple, what annual rate of interest is implied by these instalments under the standard average-due-date method? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"₹18,000 का ऋण ₹1,800 की 11 समान मासिक किश्तों में चुकाया जाता है, जो पहले महीने से प्रारंभ होकर क्रमागत महीनों के अंत में देय हैं। यदि ब्याज साधारण है, तो मानक औसत-देय-तिथि विधि के अंतर्गत इन किश्तों द्वारा निहित वार्षिक ब्याज दर क्या है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20%"},"2":{"en":"18%"},"3":{"en":"22%"},"4":{"en":"24%"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Total repayment = \\(1800 \\times 11 = 19800\\)<br>Interest paid = \\(19800 - 18000 = 1800\\)<br>Average due date of 11 monthly instalments = mean of 1 to 11 months = 6 months = \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) year<br>\\(1800 = \\frac{18000 \\times R \\times \\frac{1}{2}}{100}\\)<br>\\(R = \\frac{1800 \\times 100}{9000} = \\boxed{20}\\)%<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 20%.</b>","hi":"कुल भुगतान = \\(1800 \\times 11 = 19800\\)<br>दिया गया ब्याज = \\(19800 - 18000 = 1800\\)<br>11 मासिक किश्तों की औसत देय तिथि = 1 से 11 महीनों का माध्य = 6 महीने = \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) वर्ष<br>\\(1800 = \\frac{18000 \\times R \\times \\frac{1}{2}}{100}\\)<br>\\(R = \\frac{1800 \\times 100}{9000} = \\boxed{20}\\)%<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 20% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000070956","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Improve the sentence by selecting the appropriate preposition from the following options.<br>The manager sent an email ___ the upcoming policy changes affecting all departments. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"regarding"},"2":{"en":"following"},"3":{"en":"through"},"4":{"en":"around"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Regarding (के बारे में) = concerning.</b><br>The email concerned upcoming policy changes affecting every department.<br>“Following” means after, “through” indicates a channel, and “around” does not express the subject.<br>“Regarding” is the precise preposition.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): regarding.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000070957","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word. <b>OBEISANCE</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Acceptance"},"2":{"en":"Worship"},"3":{"en":"Bow"},"4":{"en":"Servitude"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Obeisance (अभिवादन) = a respectful bow or gesture of deference.</b><br><b>Acceptance (स्वीकृति)</b> = agreement<br><b>Worship (पूजा)</b> = religious reverence<br><b>Bow (झुककर अभिवादन)</b> = bend the body respectfully ✔<br><b>Servitude (गुलामी)</b> = state of being enslaved; synonyms: homage, deference.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Bow.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000070958","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Convert the below given passive voice sentence into active voice.<br>“The classrooms were decorated by the students for Independence Day celebrations”. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The students decorate the classrooms for Independence Day celebrations"},"2":{"en":"The students are decorating the classrooms for Independence Day celebrations"},"3":{"en":"The students have decorated the classrooms for Independence Day celebrations"},"4":{"en":"The students decorated the classrooms for Independence Day celebrations"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Simple past passive becomes simple past active.</b><br>The agent “the students” becomes the subject.<br>“Were decorated” becomes “decorated,” with the purpose phrase unchanged.<br>The other options change tense or aspect.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): The students decorated the classrooms for Independence Day celebrations.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000070959","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Select the correctly spelt word meaning “a person who loves and collects books”. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Biblophile"},"2":{"en":"Bibliophyle"},"3":{"en":"Bibliophile"},"4":{"en":"Biblicfeal"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Bibliophile (पुस्तक-प्रेमी) = a person who loves and collects books.</b><br>The correct spelling is “bibliophile.”<br><b>Biblophile</b> omits “i”; <b>bibliophyle</b> uses “y.”<br><b>Biblicfeal</b> is not the required word.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Bibliophile.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000070960","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Four parts of a sentence are given below in a jumbled order. When arranged correctly, they form a complete and meaningful sentence. While multiple combinations may appear grammatically correct, choose the one that best conveys the intended meaning as per the given options.<br>A) aims to position<br>B) the country as a global leader<br>C) on artificial intelligence<br>D) India's National Strategy [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A-D-C-B"},"2":{"en":"C-B-D-A"},"3":{"en":"B-D-C-A"},"4":{"en":"D-A-B-C"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: D-A-B-C</b><br>D supplies the subject: India’s National Strategy.<br>A and B state its aim of positioning the country as a global leader.<br>C identifies the field: artificial intelligence.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): D-A-B-C.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000070961","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Identify the misspelt word: [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Entrepreneur"},"2":{"en":"Surveillance"},"3":{"en":"Judgement"},"4":{"en":"Embarrasment"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Embarrassment (शर्मिंदगी) = a feeling of awkwardness or shame.</b><br><b>Embarrasment</b> omits one “s.”<br><b>Entrepreneur</b> = business founder; <b>surveillance</b> = close observation.<br><b>Judgement</b> is an accepted British spelling.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Embarrasment.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000070962","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"What is the one-word substitute for:<br>“A person who pretends to be knowledgeable or skilled but is actually a fraud.” [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Savant"},"2":{"en":"Virtuoso"},"3":{"en":"Charlatan"},"4":{"en":"Visionary"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Charlatan (ढोंगी) = a fraud claiming special knowledge or skill.</b><br><b>Savant (विद्वान)</b> = learned person<br><b>Virtuoso (कुशल कलाकार)</b> = highly skilled performer<br><b>Visionary (दूरदर्शी)</b> = person with imaginative foresight<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Charlatan.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000070963","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"What is the antonym of the word “mendacious”? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Truthful"},"2":{"en":"Hidden"},"3":{"en":"Joyful"},"4":{"en":"Depressed"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Mendacious (मिथ्यावादी) = dishonest or untruthful.</b><br><b>Truthful (सत्यवादी)</b> = honest ✔<br><b>Hidden (छिपा)</b> = concealed<br><b>Joyful (आनंदित)</b> = happy; <b>depressed (उदास)</b> = dejected.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Truthful.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000070964","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom given below:<br>“Ride roughshod over” [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Treat with extreme care"},"2":{"en":"Disregard others’ rights or feelings"},"3":{"en":"Assist someone compassionately"},"4":{"en":"Move slowly"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Ride roughshod over (अनादर से दबाना) = treat without regard for rights or feelings.</b><br>Example: “The management rode roughshod over the workers’ concerns.”<br>Care and compassionate assistance are opposite ideas.<br>The idiom does not mean moving slowly.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Disregard others’ rights or feelings.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000070965","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the most appropriate option:<br>No strategy was found to be ___ than diversification during the crisis. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"effective"},"2":{"en":"most effective"},"3":{"en":"more effective"},"4":{"en":"effectively"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Than” requires the comparative adjective “more effective.”</b><br>Diversification was more effective than every other strategy during the crisis.<br>The positive and superlative forms do not fit “than.”<br>“Effectively” is an adverb, but an adjective is required.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): more effective.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000070966","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the most appropriate option:<br>The treaty was hailed as a breakthrough despite its ___ language that allowed for multiple interpretations. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"ambiguous"},"2":{"en":"concise"},"3":{"en":"forthright"},"4":{"en":"implicit"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Ambiguous (अनेकार्थी) = open to multiple interpretations.</b><br>The treaty’s ambiguous language allowed different readings.<br>“Concise” means brief, “forthright” means direct, and “implicit” means implied.<br>Only “ambiguous” directly matches the explanation.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): ambiguous.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000070967","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"What is meant by the idiom “In hot water”? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To experience a sudden burst of energy"},"2":{"en":"To relax and enjoy oneself"},"3":{"en":"To be in trouble"},"4":{"en":"To seek advice from someone"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>In hot water (मुसीबत में) = in trouble.</b><br>Example: “He was in hot water after missing the deadline.”<br>Energy, relaxation and seeking advice are not expressed by the idiom.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): To be in trouble.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000070968","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the underlined part of the sentence. If the sentence is already correct, select “No substitution required”.<br>He explained the concept so <b>precise</b> that everyone grasped it immediately. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"precisely"},"2":{"en":"precision"},"3":{"en":"precised"},"4":{"en":"No substitution required"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The verb “explained” is modified by the adverb “precisely.”</b><br>Correct sentence: “He explained the concept so <b>precisely</b> that everyone grasped it immediately.”<br>“Precise” is an adjective and “precision” a noun.<br>“Precised” is not the required form.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): precisely.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000070969","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful passage.<br>1. Final budget was uploaded to the department portal.<br>2. Initial estimates were gathered from field officers.<br>3. Proposals were revised based on input.<br>4. The finance team consolidated the entries. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2-3-4-1"},"2":{"en":"2-4-3-1"},"3":{"en":"1-3-4-2"},"4":{"en":"3-2-4-1"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 2-4-3-1</b><br>Field estimates are gathered and then consolidated by the finance team.<br>Proposals are revised using the resulting input.<br>The final budget is uploaded last.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 2-4-3-1.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000070970","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage and answer the questions based on the passage:<br><br>Over the past few years, Indian destination weddings have grown into a thriving economic trend, pushing the traditional boundaries between festivals and enterprises. Exclusive domain of royal dynasties and Bollywood royalty earlier, today, such grand affairs are aspiring to be undertaken by a new generation of prosperous businesspeople and NRIs. Udaipur, Jaipur, and Kovalam have become top locations, providing a carefully designed synthesis of history, hospitality, and spectacle.<br><br>The ripple effect of such weddings on the economy is profound. A single lavish wedding can create a supply chain from hotels to caterers to artisans to transportation providers and even bouquet sellers in the neighbourhood. Industry estimates place the Indian wedding industry's contribution at close to 3.7 lakh crore each year, with destination weddings making up a large portion of it.<br><br>But there are conditions. Local infrastructure gets strained during peak season, especially in small towns that have not been designed for high-density tourism. Furthermore, environmental issues—such as over-exploitation of resources, waste, and energy use—are not addressed adequately. State governments are keen on the economic boost, but regulatory frameworks do not keep pace, being set more to facilitate business than ensure sustainability.<br><br>Essentially, Indian destination weddings walk the tightrope between cultural spectacle and business venture. The economic impetus that they generate in the short term is certain, but concerns regarding their ecological impact as well as their inclusivity persist to command policy scrutiny.<br><br><br>What does the passage primarily emphasize about destination weddings in India? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"They are losing popularity"},"2":{"en":"They burden urban spaces"},"3":{"en":"They are eco-friendly"},"4":{"en":"They combine culture and commerce"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: Destination weddings walk the tightrope between cultural spectacle and business venture.</b><br>They combine historical and cultural display with major economic activity.<br>The passage does not say they are losing popularity or are eco-friendly.<br>Urban burden is only one concern, not the central emphasis.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): They combine culture and commerce.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000070971","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage and answer the questions based on the passage:<br><br>Over the past few years, Indian destination weddings have grown into a thriving economic trend, pushing the traditional boundaries between festivals and enterprises. Exclusive domain of royal dynasties and Bollywood royalty earlier, today, such grand affairs are aspiring to be undertaken by a new generation of prosperous businesspeople and NRIs. Udaipur, Jaipur, and Kovalam have become top locations, providing a carefully designed synthesis of history, hospitality, and spectacle.<br><br>The ripple effect of such weddings on the economy is profound. A single lavish wedding can create a supply chain from hotels to caterers to artisans to transportation providers and even bouquet sellers in the neighbourhood. Industry estimates place the Indian wedding industry's contribution at close to 3.7 lakh crore each year, with destination weddings making up a large portion of it.<br><br>But there are conditions. Local infrastructure gets strained during peak season, especially in small towns that have not been designed for high-density tourism. Furthermore, environmental issues—such as over-exploitation of resources, waste, and energy use—are not addressed adequately. State governments are keen on the economic boost, but regulatory frameworks do not keep pace, being set more to facilitate business than ensure sustainability.<br><br>Essentially, Indian destination weddings walk the tightrope between cultural spectacle and business venture. The economic impetus that they generate in the short term is certain, but concerns regarding their ecological impact as well as their inclusivity persist to command policy scrutiny.<br><br><br>Which of the following best describes the tone of the author in the passage? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Sarcastic"},"2":{"en":"Analytical"},"3":{"en":"Indifferent"},"4":{"en":"Euphoric"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Analytical = examining benefits and drawbacks objectively.</b><br>The author weighs economic gains against infrastructural and environmental costs.<br>There is no sustained sarcasm, indifference or euphoria.<br>Policy implications are assessed in a measured tone.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Analytical.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000070972","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage and answer the questions based on the passage:<br><br>Over the past few years, Indian destination weddings have grown into a thriving economic trend, pushing the traditional boundaries between festivals and enterprises. Exclusive domain of royal dynasties and Bollywood royalty earlier, today, such grand affairs are aspiring to be undertaken by a new generation of prosperous businesspeople and NRIs. Udaipur, Jaipur, and Kovalam have become top locations, providing a carefully designed synthesis of history, hospitality, and spectacle.<br><br>The ripple effect of such weddings on the economy is profound. A single lavish wedding can create a supply chain from hotels to caterers to artisans to transportation providers and even bouquet sellers in the neighbourhood. Industry estimates place the Indian wedding industry's contribution at close to 3.7 lakh crore each year, with destination weddings making up a large portion of it.<br><br>But there are conditions. Local infrastructure gets strained during peak season, especially in small towns that have not been designed for high-density tourism. Furthermore, environmental issues—such as over-exploitation of resources, waste, and energy use—are not addressed adequately. State governments are keen on the economic boost, but regulatory frameworks do not keep pace, being set more to facilitate business than ensure sustainability.<br><br>Essentially, Indian destination weddings walk the tightrope between cultural spectacle and business venture. The economic impetus that they generate in the short term is certain, but concerns regarding their ecological impact as well as their inclusivity persist to command policy scrutiny.<br><br><br>Which of the following best illustrates the paradox of destination weddings, as discussed in the passage? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"They are economically beneficial but culturally irrelevant"},"2":{"en":"They promote tradition but discourage tourism"},"3":{"en":"They boost the economy but strain local resources"},"4":{"en":"They reduce employment but raise income levels"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: Weddings generate economic activity while straining infrastructure and resources.</b><br>The paradox is prosperity accompanied by local ecological and infrastructural pressure.<br>The passage affirms cultural relevance, tourism and employment.<br>Only C captures both sides.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): They boost the economy but strain local resources.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000070973","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage and answer the questions based on the passage:<br><br>Over the past few years, Indian destination weddings have grown into a thriving economic trend, pushing the traditional boundaries between festivals and enterprises. Exclusive domain of royal dynasties and Bollywood royalty earlier, today, such grand affairs are aspiring to be undertaken by a new generation of prosperous businesspeople and NRIs. Udaipur, Jaipur, and Kovalam have become top locations, providing a carefully designed synthesis of history, hospitality, and spectacle.<br><br>The ripple effect of such weddings on the economy is profound. A single lavish wedding can create a supply chain from hotels to caterers to artisans to transportation providers and even bouquet sellers in the neighbourhood. Industry estimates place the Indian wedding industry's contribution at close to 3.7 lakh crore each year, with destination weddings making up a large portion of it.<br><br>But there are conditions. Local infrastructure gets strained during peak season, especially in small towns that have not been designed for high-density tourism. Furthermore, environmental issues—such as over-exploitation of resources, waste, and energy use—are not addressed adequately. State governments are keen on the economic boost, but regulatory frameworks do not keep pace, being set more to facilitate business than ensure sustainability.<br><br>Essentially, Indian destination weddings walk the tightrope between cultural spectacle and business venture. The economic impetus that they generate in the short term is certain, but concerns regarding their ecological impact as well as their inclusivity persist to command policy scrutiny.<br><br><br>Why does the author mention regulatory mechanisms in the context of destination weddings? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To highlight efficient government intervention"},"2":{"en":"To show the decline of legal oversight"},"3":{"en":"To critique the lack of sustainability focus"},"4":{"en":"To explain GST complications"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: Regulations facilitate business more than they ensure sustainability.</b><br>The author criticizes their failure to address environmental concerns adequately.<br>Efficient intervention is not claimed, and GST is not discussed.<br>The point is a sustainability deficit, not merely declining oversight.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): To critique the lack of sustainability focus.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000070974","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage and answer the questions based on the passage:<br><br>Over the past few years, Indian destination weddings have grown into a thriving economic trend, pushing the traditional boundaries between festivals and enterprises. Exclusive domain of royal dynasties and Bollywood royalty earlier, today, such grand affairs are aspiring to be undertaken by a new generation of prosperous businesspeople and NRIs. Udaipur, Jaipur, and Kovalam have become top locations, providing a carefully designed synthesis of history, hospitality, and spectacle.<br><br>The ripple effect of such weddings on the economy is profound. A single lavish wedding can create a supply chain from hotels to caterers to artisans to transportation providers and even bouquet sellers in the neighbourhood. Industry estimates place the Indian wedding industry's contribution at close to 3.7 lakh crore each year, with destination weddings making up a large portion of it.<br><br>But there are conditions. Local infrastructure gets strained during peak season, especially in small towns that have not been designed for high-density tourism. Furthermore, environmental issues—such as over-exploitation of resources, waste, and energy use—are not addressed adequately. State governments are keen on the economic boost, but regulatory frameworks do not keep pace, being set more to facilitate business than ensure sustainability.<br><br>Essentially, Indian destination weddings walk the tightrope between cultural spectacle and business venture. The economic impetus that they generate in the short term is certain, but concerns regarding their ecological impact as well as their inclusivity persist to command policy scrutiny.<br><br><br>What is the author's central recommendation regarding destination weddings and public policy? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Encourage more private investment"},"2":{"en":"Limit weddings to off-season only"},"3":{"en":"Integrate sustainability into regulation"},"4":{"en":"Promote international venues instead"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>The passage calls for policy scrutiny of ecological impact and sustainability.</b><br>Regulation should balance economic growth with environmental responsibility.<br>Private investment, off-season restrictions and international venues are not recommended.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Integrate sustainability into regulation.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000070975","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word: <b>DISINGENUOUS</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Naive"},"2":{"en":"Deceitful"},"3":{"en":"Honest"},"4":{"en":"Open"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Disingenuous (कपटपूर्ण) = insincere or deceitful.</b><br><b>Naive (भोला)</b> = inexperienced or innocent<br><b>Deceitful (धोखेबाज)</b> = dishonest ✔<br><b>Honest (ईमानदार)</b> = truthful; <b>open (खुला)</b> = frank; synonyms: insincere, duplicitous.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Deceitful.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000070976","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word. <b>Trivial</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Insignificant"},"2":{"en":"Vital"},"3":{"en":"Petty"},"4":{"en":"Small"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Trivial (तुच्छ) = unimportant.</b><br><b>Insignificant (महत्वहीन)</b> = unimportant<br><b>Vital (अत्यावश्यक)</b> = essential ✔<br><b>Petty (तुच्छ)</b> = minor; <b>small (छोटा)</b> = little; other antonyms: significant, crucial.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Vital.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000070977","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Spot the correct spelling of a word meaning “impossible to compare”. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Incommensurabel"},"2":{"en":"Incomensurable"},"3":{"en":"Incommensurable"},"4":{"en":"Incommensuarable"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Incommensurable (अतुलनीय) = impossible to compare by a common standard.</b><br>The correct spelling is “incommensurable.”<br><b>Incommensurabel</b> reverses the ending; <b>incomensurable</b> omits “m.”<br><b>Incommensuarable</b> incorrectly inserts “a.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Incommensurable.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000070978","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct one-word substitute for: “One who is indifferent to pleasure or pain”. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"ascetic"},"2":{"en":"Skeptic"},"3":{"en":"Optimist"},"4":{"en":"Masochist"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Ascetic (तपस्वी) = one who practises severe self-discipline and abstains from indulgence.</b><br>The ascetic remains detached from pleasure and pain.<br><b>Skeptic (संशयवादी)</b> = doubter<br><b>Optimist (आशावादी)</b> = hopeful person; <b>masochist</b> = one who derives gratification from pain<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): ascetic.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000070979","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Select the sentence containing the homonym of the highlighted word:<br>He offered his <b>resignation</b> without protest. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Her face showed resignation to fate."},"2":{"en":"The resignation letter was printed."},"3":{"en":"They accepted his resignation."},"4":{"en":"The manager signed the resignation note."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Resignation = leaving a job, or acceptance of something unavoidable.</b><br>The original concerns resigning from a position.<br>Option A uses “resignation” for acceptance of fate.<br>The other options retain the employment meaning.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Her face showed resignation to fate.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000070980","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences to form a coherent paragraph:<br>1. The most prevalent of these is the peer review process, where a manuscript is evaluated by other experts in the same field.<br>2. The integrity of scientific publications is upheld by a series of rigorous checks and balances.<br>3. The goal of this process is to validate the methodology, findings, and conclusions of the research before it is made public.<br>4. This external scrutiny helps to ensure that only high-quality, credible research is disseminated to the scientific community. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2,1,3,4"},"2":{"en":"1,2,3,4"},"3":{"en":"3,4,1,2"},"4":{"en":"4,3,2,1"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 2-1-3-4</b><br>Sentence 2 introduces checks on scientific integrity, and sentence 1 identifies peer review.<br>Sentence 3 states the goal of peer review.<br>Sentence 4 concludes with the benefit of external scrutiny.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 2,1,3,4.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};